{"row_key": "S6_01_INVARIANTS:A2.1", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "inv:A2.1", "source_file": "fragments/part_A.tex, Statement A2.1", "source_line": 2821, "source_section": "The cotangent direct images and the decisive period scalar", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[The complete raw period determinant]\label{inv:A2.1}\label{wb:prop:log-ks-divisor}\label{wb:prop:period-derivative-determinant}
On the marked upper half-plane,
\begin{equation}\label{inv:eq:A-modular-K}
6\mu_z^2-\tau_z\beta_z
=\tau_z^2\frac{E_4(\tau)^2}{E_6(\tau)}.
\end{equation}
The right side extends holomorphically through the apparent poles.
Its exact orders are two at $z_1$ and zero at $z_2$; it has no other
zero away from their translates.  The logarithmic connecting map
$\kappa_0:f_*\mathcal E\to\mathcal L\otimes G$ has divisor
$\operatorname{divisor}(\det\kappa_0)=p_1+p_2$.
