{"row_key": "S6_01_INVARIANTS:A2.3", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "inv:A2.3", "source_file": "fragments/part_A.tex, Statement A2.3", "source_line": 3013, "source_section": "The cotangent direct images and the decisive period scalar", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Identification of the elliptic logarithm and the verified zero formula]\label{inv:A2.3}
For the Weierstrass equation
\[
y^2=x^3-3t^3(t-1)x+2t^4(t-1)^2,
\]
the section $[\mu]$ is a generator of its rational section group and
equals one of $P_*=(0,\sqrt2t^2(t-1))$ and $-P_*$.
In particular $\wp(\mu,\tau)=0$ on every regular fibre.
Along the branch in \eqref{inv:eq:A-s-branch}, with
$x_0=1-1/t$, the exact branch is
\begin{equation}\label{inv:eq:A-DI-branch}
\mu=\frac{1-\tau}{2}
 +\frac{i\sqrt6}{3\pi}
 \frac{x_0^{1/4}\,{}_3F_2(1/3,2/3,1;3/4,5/4;x_0)}
 {{}_2F_1(1/12,5/12;1;1-x_0)}.
\end{equation}
Consequently $\mu-(2-\tau)/3$ has exact order two at the
order-three point in $r^3=t$.
