{"row_key": "S6_01_INVARIANTS:C3.2", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "inv:C3.2", "source_file": "fragments/part_C.tex, Statement C3.2", "source_line": 4419, "source_section": "Fr\"olicher, Bott--Chern, Aeppli, and Hermitian metrics", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[The factor $12$ with a fixed collar orientation]\label{inv:C3.2}\label{wb:lem:bcpr-degree-one-input}
Use the marked cohomology class $\gamma$ dual to
$\hat\gamma$, the analytic peripheral generators and the lift relation of
[AC26, Section 7.5], and put
$p=12l_0-4l_1-3l_2=\pm1$.  Let $g_\gamma$ be the unique coherent
Leray class whose fibre image is $\gamma^{0,1}$.  Then
\begin{equation}\label{inv:eq:C-factor12}
\exp(12g_\gamma)=f^*\OO_{\Pone}(-p).
\end{equation}
For the standard data $(l_0,l_1,l_2)=(0,1,-1)$, this is
$\exp(12g_\gamma)=f^*\OO(1)$.  For the opposite value $p=1$,
the exponent representing $f^*\OO(1)$ is $-12g_\gamma$.
