{"row_key": "S6_01_INVARIANTS:C3.6", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "inv:C3.6", "source_file": "fragments/part_C.tex, Statement C3.6", "source_line": 4655, "source_section": "Fr\"olicher, Bott--Chern, Aeppli, and Hermitian metrics", "placement_basis": "inventory kind and plan condition 2", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Cited/re-derived", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Gauduchon metrics with specified Chern--Ricci form]\label{inv:C3.6}
There exists a Gauduchon metric on $X$.  More precisely, for every
Gauduchon metric $\omega_0$ there is another Gauduchon metric
$\omega$ with $[\omega^2]_A=[\omega_0^2]_A$ and
\begin{equation}\label{inv:eq:C-Ricci}
\operatorname{Ric}^{\mathrm{Ch}}(\omega)=\pi f^*\omega_{FS}.
\end{equation}
This Ricci form is semipositive and has rank one at regular points
of $f$.  No Chern--Ricci-flat Hermitian metric exists on $X$.
