{"row_key": "S6_01_INVARIANTS:E1.1", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "inv:E1.1", "source_file": "fragments/part_E.tex, E1.1", "source_line": 52662, "source_section": "Comb invariants and the precise vector-field correction", "placement_basis": "inventory kind and plan condition 2", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Cited/re-derived", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Credited re-derivation: stability of the pencil for the standard family]\label{inv:E1.1}
Every sufficiently small deformation of the standard $X_c$ carries a
holomorphic map to $\Pone$ with general fibre a complex two-torus. Its
complete anticanonical system $|-2K|$ is basepoint-free of dimension one
and recovers that map, and its algebraic dimension is one.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "found_in_checked_scope; AC2026, Theorem9.1(i),(iii), original pp64–65. Algebraic reduction a(X)=1 and the original canonical formula are already proved. These assertions do not by themselves prove completeness of all small deformations. Actual scope/search record: work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_comparison_5.json#E1.1.", "found_in_E26": "not_found_in_checked_scope; Engel2026, S6.tex1647–1671; main-thm882–908. The actual one-parameter holomorphic family and its algebraic dimension1 appear, but neither its miniversality nor the full intrinsic |-2K| stability conclusion was identified in the checked passages/searches. Actual scope/search record: work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_comparison_5.json#E1.1.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "found_in_checked_scope; DuEtAl2026v1, Theorem1.3 at310–321; Proposition6.16 at9876–9919; Theorem7.1 at10018–10103. The actual period family is locally miniversal, and every member has K^(-2)=f*O(1), exactly two base sections and a basepoint-free pencil recovering f. Together with the already proved algebraic-dimension statement this yields the entire receiving stability assertion. It is an immediate combined consequence, not a new miniversality theorem. Actual scope/search record: work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_comparison_5.json#E1.1.", "found_elsewhere": "found_in_checked_scope; ViaclovskyCombs2026, Proposition9.2, source2516–2551, compiled p31: The same vertical-divisor/Kähler-fibre argument is proved for each comb family member; it supplies a published-method comparison, not miniversality of the standard family. DGKXv2: No full stability/miniversality/pencil statement identified in this separately checked version. The v1 theorem scopes must not be transferred to v2. Exact bounded scopes in work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_comparison_5.json#E1.1."}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Every sufficiently small deformation of the standard X_c retains the basepoint-free pencil |-2K|, a torus fibration over P1, and algebraic dimension one. | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: Proof uses completeness of the actual family; semicontinuity alone is explicitly not used to lift sections. | proof_sha256: c2ec633d0ed187b0d079125c5c222f21d7598312fa81b0e6a41b18a00cc710f0 | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json. | Final scoped credit/status closure: work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_inventory_overlay_5.json; Attribution-only update by GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, 17 November2026UTC; existing full proof checks unchanged. No global absence/priority claim."}

{"row_key": "S6_01_INVARIANTS:E2.4", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "inv:E2.4", "source_file": "fragments/part_E.tex, E2.4", "source_line": 52886, "source_section": "Comb invariants and the precise vector-field correction", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Counterexample", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Counterexample: The universal two-vector-field bound]\label{inv:E2.4}
