\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "found_in_checked_scope; AC2026, Remark1.2 p4; Remark9.26 p83. The unrestricted HKP bound is repeated as compatible with the original example h0(T)=1. This is the prior assertion being refuted, not a prior proof of the comb counterexample. Actual scope/search record: work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_comparison_5.json#E2.4.", "found_in_E26": "not_found_in_checked_scope; Engel2026, Introduction211–240; main-thm882–908; family remark1647–1671. No universal two-vector-field bound or comb refutation identified in the exact checked original construction/family passages and saved vector-field/comb searches. Actual scope/search record: work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_comparison_5.json#E2.4.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "found_in_checked_scope; DuEtAl2026v1, Theorem1.3 at310–316; exact tangent theorem6.12. The standard-family h0(T)=1 statement is proved, but it is not the universal bound or its comb refutation. No comb construction occurs in the recorded search. Actual scope/search record: work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_comparison_5.json#E2.4.", "found_elsewhere": "found_in_checked_scope; HKP2000, Original preprint p2, Corollary1.3 and complete proof: Corollary1.3 states h0(T)<=2 for any complex structure on S6. Its complete proof uses CDP1998 constancy of all meromorphic coefficients. The current torus fibration supplies nonconstant functions, so that implication cannot establish this bound here. The refutation uses the separately checked exact comb vector-field count, not merely criticism of the old proof. | ViaclovskyCombs2026, Theorem1.1; source2639–2674: The actual comb manifolds and the separate evaluation-rank bound<=2 are present; the latter does not bound the dimension of the whole space of vector fields. No exact h0(T)=2m+1/refutation is claimed from this original. DGKXv2: No universal bound or its comb refutation identified in this version’s checked scope/searches. Exact bounded scopes in work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_comparison_5.json#E2.4."}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: The universal bound h0(T)<=2 in HKP Corollary1.3, repeated in AC26 Remark9.26, is false for the comb members, whose h0(T)=2m+1>=25. | SOURCE STATUS: Refuted | SOURCE NOTES: Exact failed step identified: invoking CDP98 to make meromorphic vector-field coefficients constant. This does not refute an a=0-restricted statement. | proof_sha256: 60c0871b6bfd74e9d8a8c7c83cff7e1927438999ac9fb52cf2d0f5313758d89e | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json. | Final scoped credit/status closure: work/invariants_arithmetic/inv_E_credit_inventory_overlay_5.json; Attribution-only update by GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, 17 November2026UTC; existing full proof checks unchanged. No global absence/priority claim."}

{"row_key": "S6_02_FAMILY:D.1.2", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "fam:src:D.1.2", "source_file": "sections/CD.tex; statement D.1.2", "source_line": 1686, "source_section": "Exceptional fibres, Neron--Severi classes, and compact subspaces", "placement_basis": "inventory kind and plan condition 2", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Cited/re-derived", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}\label{fam:src:D.1.2}\label{fam:st:D.1.2}
The locus on \(B^\circ\) where \(P(t)\) is torsion is countable and dense.
Every fibre over this locus is an abelian surface. The divisor on the
smooth base cut out by \(6kP=O\) has degree \(3k^2-1\), including local
intersection multiplicity, for every positive integer \(k\).
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "No matching additional assertion located in the original-PDF comparison of Sections2–7 and9–10 for this result; period/finite-filling/cusp/cohomology terms searched in its transcription. Construction and standard invariants are credited separately. Compared assertion: Dense countable torsion locus; abelian torsion fibres; degree 3k^2-1", "found_in_E26": "Found: Lemma2.1 supplies the section height and intersection inputs; torsion-fibre product isogeny is derived in full.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "No matching additional assertion located in the main statements, Sections6–7 or AppendixC for this result. Classification, tangent, Kuranishi, automorphism and coherent-closing overlaps are separately attributed; version2 was searched for the same scope. Compared assertion: Dense countable torsion locus; abelian torsion fibres; degree 3k^2-1", "found_elsewhere": "Matched the exact external statements cited in the complete proof against the opened-source ledger. Nearby Yang, Wang, Viaclovsky and Liu–Rollenske families were compared in their stated scope; no wider result is attributed to them. Compared assertion: Dense countable torsion locus; abelian torsion fibres; degree 3k^2-1"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Dense countable torsion locus; abelian torsion fibres; degree 3k^2-1 | SOURCE STATUS: Known | SOURCE NOTES: Own Betti-map and product-cover proofs; degree derived from Engel Lemma2.1 height computation."}

{"row_key": "S6_02_FAMILY:D.1.3", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "fam:src:D.1.3", "source_file": "sections/CD.tex; statement D.1.3", "source_line": 1698, "source_section": "Exceptional fibres, Neron--Severi classes, and compact subspaces", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Counterexample", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}[counterexample]\label{fam:src:D.1.3}\label{fam:st:D.1.3}
