{"row_key": "S6_02_FAMILY:D.2.1", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "fam:src:D.2.1", "source_file": "sections/CD.tex; statement D.2.1", "source_line": 1919, "source_section": "Exceptional fibres, Neron--Severi classes, and compact subspaces", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}\label{fam:src:D.2.1}\label{fam:st:D.2.1}
For a standard-twist member \(X_c\) with underlying manifold \(S^6\),
every compact irreducible complex curve lies in one fibre of \(f\), and
every compact irreducible complex surface is one of the reduced fibres.
