{"row_key": "S6_02_FAMILY:F.2.3", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "fam:src:F.2.3", "source_file": "sections/F.tex F.2.3", "source_line": 2352, "source_section": "The monodromy group and its period domain", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}\label{fam:src:F.2.3}\label{fam:st:F.2.3}
The positive sign region admits the global period chart
\[
 \mathcal O_+=\left\{
 (\tau,\mu,\beta)\in\mathbb C^3:
 \operatorname{Im}\tau>0,\quad
 \operatorname{Im}\beta-\frac{6(\operatorname{Im}\mu)^2}
 {\operatorname{Im}\tau}<0\right\},
\]
represented by the matrix $\Pi$ in the stated problem.  In this chart,
\begin{equation}\label{fam:eq:F-qD}
 q_e(J)=-\frac6D.
\end{equation}
Every admissible period $\Pi_c(z)$ belongs to $\mathcal O_+$, for every
admissible $c$.  Thus this single maximal proper-action open set contains
all the period images in question.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "No matching additional assertion located in the original-PDF comparison of Sections2–7 and9–10 for this result; period/finite-filling/cusp/cohomology terms searched in its transcription. Construction and standard invariants are credited separately. Compared assertion: The positive component is the global tau-mu-beta chart with Im tau positive and D negative; q_delta=-6/D and all admissible periods lie there.", "found_in_E26": "No matching additional assertion located in Sections2–8, especially Lemma2.1, Construction3.5, Theorem5.1 and Remarks8.1–8.4, for this result. Elliptic-surface construction and section-height input are credited where used. Compared assertion: The positive component is the global tau-mu-beta chart with Im tau positive and D negative; q_delta=-6/D and all admissible periods lie there.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "No matching additional assertion located in the main statements, Sections6–7 or AppendixC for this result. Classification, tangent, Kuranishi, automorphism and coherent-closing overlaps are separately attributed; version2 was searched for the same scope. Compared assertion: The positive component is the global tau-mu-beta chart with Im tau positive and D negative; q_delta=-6/D and all admissible periods lie there.", "found_elsewhere": "Matched the exact external statements cited in the complete proof against the opened-source ledger. Nearby Yang, Wang, Viaclovsky and Liu–Rollenske families were compared in their stated scope; no wider result is attributed to them. Compared assertion: The positive component is the global tau-mu-beta chart with Im tau positive and D negative; q_delta=-6/D and all admissible periods lie there."}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: The positive component is the global tau-mu-beta chart with Im tau positive and D negative; q_delta=-6/D and all admissible periods lie there. | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: Exact typed compariso