{"row_key": "S6_02_PUSH:C.3.3", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "push:src:C.3.3", "source_file": "sections/C_push.tex;code/c_exact.py", "source_line": 41827, "source_section": "Known source results and complete re-derivations", "placement_basis": "inventory kind and plan condition 2", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Cited/re-derived", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[equivariance alone is insufficient]\label{push:src:C.3.3}
All 28 oriented mapping classes of $S^6$ admit representatives
equivariant for one fixed semifree circle action with fixed set $S^2$.
Consequently the circle action, its fixed set, and its normal weights
do not determine $[\Phi]$.
