{"row_key": "S6_02_PUSH:D.3.2", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "push:src:D.3.2", "source_file": "sections/D_push.tex D.3.2", "source_line": 23177, "source_section": "The boundary of the parameter disc", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Corollary", "source_statement": "\begin{corollary}\label{push:src:D.3.2}
There is no path-independent limiting group at the boundary even
when \(c_n\to c_*\) from the admissible side. At \(h_n=0\) and
\(c_n=c_*-i\epsilon_n\), all of \(L_a\) survives, giving a
three-dimensional real torus if \(a\) is rational and a
two-dimensional real torus if \(a\) is irrational. Other admissible
paths give a point. The fixed-boundary Hausdorff reflection of \ref{push:src:D.2.3}
therefore cannot be identified with all pointed fibre limits.
\end{corollary}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "No matching additional assertion located in the original-PDF comparison of Sections2–7 and9–10 for this result; period/finite-filling/cusp/cohomology terms searched in its transcription. Construction and standard invariants are credited separately. Compared assertion: Admissible paths can yield different limiting torus dimensions, so no path-independent local group limit exists.", "found_in_E26": "No matching additional assertion located in Sections2–8, especially Lemma2.1, Construction3.5, Theorem5.1 and Remarks8.1–8.4, for this result. Elliptic-surface construction and section-height input are credited where used. Compared assertion: Admissible paths can yield different limiting torus dimensions, so no path-independent local group limit exists.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "No matching additional assertion located in the main statements, Sections6–7 or AppendixC for this result. Classification, tangent, Kuranishi, automorphism and coherent-closing overlaps are separately attributed; version2 was searched for the same scope. Compared assertion: Admissible paths can yield different limiting torus dimensions, so no path-independent local group limit exists.", "found_elsewhere": "Matched the exact external statements cited in the complete proof against the opened-source ledger. Nearby Yang, Wang, Viaclovsky and Liu–Rollenske families were compared in their stated scope; no wider result is attributed to them. Compared assertion: Admissible paths can yield different limiting torus dimensions, so no path-independent local group limit exists."}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Admissible paths can yield different limiting torus dimensions, so no path-independent local group limit exists. | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: Ordinary base points retain their nonsingular complex limits.", "pre_current_event_status": "historical record: Proved; current-writing proof review pending", "current_event