{"row_key": "S6_02_PUSH:E.2.3", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "push:src:E.2.3", "source_file": "sections/E_push.tex", "source_line": 24483, "source_section": "Classification and deformation questions", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[separation in irreducible analytic families]\label{push:src:E.2.3}
Suppose a proper holomorphic submersion over a connected
irreducible reduced complex base has two fibres of the type
in \ref{push:src:E.2.1}.  Then their multiplicity pairs agree, even if some
other fibres have not been constructed by this method.
For these members the asymptotic number
\[
 s(X)=\lim_{r\to\infty}
 \frac{h^0(X,K_X^r)-h^0(X,K_X^{-r})}{r}
 =\frac1{12}-\frac1{3k}-\frac1{4l}
\]
recovers the ordered multiplicity pair uniquely.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "No matching additional assertion located in the original-PDF comparison of Sections2–7 and9–10 for this result; period/finite-filling/cusp/cohomology terms searched in its transcription. Construction and standard invariants are credited separately. Compared assertion: Different multiplicity pairs cannot occur in one proper holomorphic submersion over a connected irreducible reduced analytic base", "found_in_E26": "No matching additional assertion located in Sections2–8, especially Lemma2.1, Construction3.5, Theorem5.1 and Remarks8.1–8.4, for this result. Elliptic-surface construction and section-height input are credited where used. Compared assertion: Different multiplicity pairs cannot occur in one proper holomorphic submersion over a connected irreducible reduced analytic base", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "No matching additional assertion located in the main statements, Sections6–7 or AppendixC for this result. Classification, tangent, Kuranishi, automorphism and coherent-closing overlaps are separately attributed; version2 was searched for the same scope. Compared assertion: Different multiplicity pairs cannot occur in one proper holomorphic submersion over a connected irreducible reduced analytic base", "found_elsewhere": "Matched the exact external statements cited in the complete proof against the opened-source ledger. Nearby Yang, Wang, Viaclovsky and Liu–Rollenske families were compared in their stated scope; no wider result is attributed to them. Compared assertion: Different multiplicity pairs cannot occur in one proper holomorphic submersion over a connected irreducible reduced analytic base"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Different multiplicity pairs cannot occur in one proper holomorphic submersion over a connected irreducible reduced analytic base | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: Signed canonical growth 1/12-1/(3k)-1/(4l) recovers m,n from the reduced fraction (m+n)/(mn)"}

{"row_key": "S6_02_PUSH:E.2.9", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "push:src:E.2.9", "source_file": "sections/E_horizontal_vanishing.tex", "source_line": 49138, "source_section": "Connected deformation chains and two independent periods", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[no horizontal divisor when all fibres are irreducible]\label{push:src:E.2.9}
Let $X$ be a compact complex threefold diffeomorphic to $S^6$,
and let $f:X\to\mathbb P^1$ be a surjective holomorphic map
with connected fibres.  If every reduced fibre is irreducible,
then $X$ has no horizontal prime divisor for $f$.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "No matching additional assertion located in the original-PDF comparison of Sections2–7 and9–10 for this result; period/finite-filling/cusp/cohomology terms searched in its transcription. Construction and standard invariants are credited separately. Compared assertion: A holomorphic connected fibration from a complex S6 with irreducible reduced fibres has no horizontal prime divisor", "found_in_E26": "No matching additional assertion located in Sections2–8, especially Lemma2.1, Construction3.5, Theorem5.1 and Remarks8.1–8.4, for this result. Elliptic-surface construction and section-height input are credited where used. Compared assertion: A holomorphic connected fibration from a complex S6 with irreducible reduced fibres has no horizontal prime divisor", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "No matching additional assertion located in the main statements, Sections6–7 or AppendixC for this result. Classification, tangent, Kuranishi, automorphism and coherent-closing overlaps are separately attributed; version2 was searched for the same scope. Compared assertion: A holomorphic connected fibration from a complex S6 with irreducible reduced fibres has no horizontal prime divisor", "found_elsewhere": "Matched the exact external statements cited in the complete proof against the opened-source ledger. Nearby Yang, Wang, Viaclovsky and Liu–Rollenske families were compared in their stated scope; no wider result is attributed to them. Compared assertion: A holomorphic connected fibration from a complex S6 with irreducible reduced fibres has no horizontal prime divisor"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: A holomorphic connected fibration from a complex S6 with irreducible reduced fibres has no horizontal prime divisor | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: D and root full-source referee PASS. Opposite Picard twists provide separate H0 and H2/H3 vanishings; one holomorphic line of additive Picard classes makes them simultaneous. This contradicts chi(TX)=1. No CDP Theorem2.2 is imported.; Subject transfer: global fibration stability and deformation chains. | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json."}

{"row_key": "S6_02_PUSH:E.4.2", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "push:src:E.4.2", "source_file": "sections/E4_push.tex; code/e4_cover_and_local.py", "source_line": 24865, "source_section": "Classification and deformation questions", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Theorem", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}[quantitative local maximum]\label{push:src:E.4.2}
