{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:A.1.1", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:A.1.1", "source_file": "sections/part_A.tex; Statement A.1.1", "source_line": 2580, "source_section": "Cotangent torsion, conductor and the printed endpoint error", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[The conormal filtration and its exact section criterion]\label{cdp:st:A.1.1}\label{wbII:prop:criterion}\label{wbII:prop:filtration}\label{wbII:lem:conormal}\label{wbII:lem:conormal-injective}\label{wbII:prop:missing-global-section-criterion}\label{wbII:prop:missing-cotangent-filtration}
The conormal map $d:N^*\to V$, defined by $[F]\mapsto dF|_S$ for a local defining equation $F$, is injective. With $K=\ker(V\to Q)$, there are canonical exact sequences
\begin{align}
0&\longrightarrow N^*\xrightarrow{d}K\longrightarrow T\longrightarrow0,
\label{cdp:A:filtration1}\\
0&\longrightarrow K\longrightarrow V\longrightarrow Q\longrightarrow0.
\label{cdp:A:filtration2}
\end{align}
Let $\partial_A:H^0(S,Q\otimes A)\to H^1(S,K\otimes A)$ and $\delta_A:H^0(S,T\otimes A)\to H^1(S,N^*\otimes A)$ be their connecting maps. Then
\[
 H^0(S,V\otimes A)=0
 \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
 H^0(S,K\otimes A)=0\ \hbox{and}\ \partial_A\hbox{ is injective}.
\tag{A.1}\label{cdp:eq:A.1}
\]
Under the explicit hypotheses $H^0(S,N^*\otimes A)=0$ and $H^0(S,Q\otimes A)=0$, $H^0(S,V\otimes A)$ is canonically $\ker\delta_A$.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["conormal", "cotangent", "torsion"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#A.1.1|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 55}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 71}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [{"baseline": "AC26", "relation": "partial_known_input", "locator": "Theorem10.5 and its proof pp88–89; section10.4 pp89–90", "comparison": "The specific normal-crossing ambient obstruction and normalization-kernel mechanism are known; the general conormal filtration, two precise vanishings and every-hypersurface formulation have broader scope."}], "relation": "The specific normal-crossing ambient obstruction and normalization-kernel mechanism are known; the general conormal filtration, two precise vanishings and every-hypersurface formulation have broader scope."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["conormal", "cotangent", "torsion"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#A.1.1|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 9}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim th