 0a172f8ef63ac14364ef5f59ba175339a4afbdc5207d40197fc59f9f8270e15f | Credit evidence (cdp_audit/result_audit.json): Granger–Schulze 2014, arXiv:1109.2612v7, Theorems 1.1/1.3, Proposition 3.4, Corollary 3.5 opened and matched; A.2.3 known; fractional-ideal identifications re-derived. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json.", "pre_current_event_status": "historical record: Proved; current-writing proof review pending", "current_event_sources": ["records/sign_events.tsv"]}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:A.2.5", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:A.2.5", "source_file": "sections/part_A.tex; Statement A.2.5", "source_line": 2731, "source_section": "Cotangent torsion, conductor and the printed endpoint error", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Vertical residue poles at a tacnode--cusp intersection]\label{cdp:st:A.2.5}
For $F=x^2-y^4z^3$, normalization is $x=u^2v^3$, $y=u$, $z=v^2$. Put $A_0=\C\{u,v^2\}$ and $B=\C\{u,v\}$. Then
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 R&=A_0\oplus u^2v^3A_0,&\mathfrak c&=u^2v^2B,\\
 J^{-1}&=A_0\oplus(uv)^{-1}A_0,&
 J^{-1}/B&\simeq A_0/(uv^2).
 \end{aligned}
 \tag{A.9a}\label{cdp:eq:A.9a}
\]
In a trivialization of $N^*$ the torsion module is
\[
 T\simeq R/(x,y^3z^2),\qquad
 \tau=2yz\,dx-4xz\,dy-3xy\,dz.
 \tag{A.9b}\label{cdp:eq:A.9b}
\]
In particular $v^{-1}\in J^{-1}\setminus B$. For the ruling with base coordinate $v$, this is a residue constant on its generic fibres with a pole on the vertical divisor $v=0$, although the horizontal conductor $u=0$ has coefficient two.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["tacnod", "residue pole", "cuspidal"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#A.2.5|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 0}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["tacnod", "residue pole", "cuspidal"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#A.2.5|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 1}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["tacnod", "residue pole", "cuspidal"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#A.2.5|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1