{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C.3.8", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C.3.8", "source_file": "sections/part_C1_C3.tex; Statement C.3.8", "source_line": 1498, "source_section": "Complete smooth-fibre classification and actual Hopf occurrence", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Proved exclusion of elliptic Hopf general fibres]\label{cdp:st:C.3.8}

The very general Hopf fibre of the algebraic reduction in \ref{cdp:st:C.3.1}
has algebraic dimension zero. In particular neither primary nor
secondary Hopf surfaces of algebraic dimension one can be its
general fibre. This exclusion uses no restriction-surjectivity
assertion from CDP98 or CDP20.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["Hopf", "algebraic.dimension", "contraction"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.3.8|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 22}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 23}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["Hopf", "algebraic.dimension", "contraction"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.3.8|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 9}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["Hopf", "algebraic.dimension", "contraction"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.3.8|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 2}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [{"citation_key": "SS2002", "relation": "cited original input or explicit comparison; not by itself a match of the full receiving statement", "source_opening_records": [{"record_file": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/references_verified.json", "key": "SS2002", "status": "verified in the specified scope", "locators": ["arXivmath/0001077v2, §1 pp2–3: degree, intrinsic Picard quotient and (d,j,alpha) coordinates", "Definition2.1 and Propositions2.4–2.6 with full proofs pp4–6", "Proposition3.1 with full contraction-normal-form proof pp6–7", "Proposition4.1 with full proof p13"], "scope": "The admissibility definition requires irreducible normal crossings, d-semistability and trivial dualizing line, without assuming an existing Kodaira smoothing. The normalized surface cases, diagonal Hopf criterion and ruled translation criterion match these hypotheses. In §1 the positive-degree class fixes the inversion ambiguity in C*.", "reader": "GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, writing run; 17 November 2026 UTC"}]}], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#C.3.8", "terms_searched": ["Hopf", "algebraic.dimension", "contraction"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Very general Hopf general fibre has algebraic dimension zero | SOURCE STATUS: Proved exclusion of elliptic Hopf general fibres | SOURCE NOTES: Elliptic Hopf surfaces have anticanonical Iitaka dimension one. Semicontinuity on a curve and a countable-union argument force a relative anticanonical system of rank at least two; this contradicts a(Y)=1. | remarks: The explicit invariant bivectors give an effective anticanonical divisor on a primary Hopf cover. Every curve is vertical, so a positive power is pulled back from a positive-degree line on P1. Finite-cover invariant rings preserve Iitaka dimension. The countable closed-analytic loci h0(K^-m)>=2 force a rank-two direct image if elliptic Hopf fibres occur very generally. | proof_sha256: 3ed35fd3f9e6ea97950eca3fb744028f04fdd77c60ce6b989b0a1ab1fb18fcb5 | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json."}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C2a", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C2a", "source_file": "sections/part_C2_C4_C5.tex; Statement C2a", "source_line": 19392, "source_section": "Normal-crossing topology and canonical-flat component comparisons", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Euler localization for torus fibrations]\label{cdp:st:C2a}
Let $g:Y\to C$ be a proper surjective holomorphic map from a connected compact complex manifold to a compact Riemann surface, with connected general fibre $F$. Let $\Sigma\subset C$ contain every critical value. Then $\Sigma$ can be chosen finite, and
\[
 e(Y)=e(C\setminus\Sigma)e(F)+\sum_{c\in\Sigma}e((Y_c)_{\rm red}). \tag{C.1}\label{cdp:eq:C.1}
\]
For a complex threefold with general fibre a complex two-torus this becomes
$\int_Yc_3(T_Y)=e(Y)=\sum_{c\in\Sigma}e((Y_c)_{\rm red})$.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["Euler", "critical.value", "localization"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C2a|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 9}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 10}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["Euler", "critical.value", "localization"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C2a|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 3}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["Euler", "critical.value", "localization"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C2a|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 40}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#C2a", "terms_searched": ["Euler", "critical.value", "localization"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Euler localization for torus fibrations | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES:  | proof_sha256: 83215d21f7ebdeb3eed046fd7d1376ec01c77b5b741d78a7905ef5f1a400d892 | remarks: Multiplicity and nilpotents do not change the underlying support Euler number. The smooth two-torus contribution is zero; the formula does not assert positivity of exceptional supports. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json."}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C2c", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C2c", "source_file": "sections/part_C2_C4_C5.tex; Statement C2c", "source_line": 19433, "source_section": "Normal-crossing topology and canonical-flat component comparisons", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Euler numbers in semistable toric rank-two models]\label{cdp:st:C2c}
Consider a rank-two Mumford model with smooth three-dimensional total space obtained from a unimodular periodic triangulation of $\R^2$, divided by a rank-two translation lattice acting freely on the total model. Let $V,E,F$ be the numbers of vertices, edges and triangles in the quotient triangulation. Its reduced central fibre has Euler number
\[
 e(S)=F=2V\in2\Z_{>0}.                                \tag{C.2}\label{cdp:eq:C.2}
\]
Every positive even number occurs in this class. A rank-one model assembled from $\PP^1$-bundles over elliptic curves with their boundary elliptic sections identified has Euler number zero.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["semistable", "toric", "Mumford"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C2c|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 52}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 58}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["semistable", "toric", "Mumford"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C2c|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 30}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["semistable", "toric", "Mumford"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C2c|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 81}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [{"citation_key": "Mumford1972", "relation": "cited original input or explicit comparison; not by itself a match of the full receiving statement", "source_opening_records": [{"record_file": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/references_verified.json", "key": "Mumford1972", "status": "verified in the specified scope", "locators": ["Entire section6, published pp264–268, including Propositions6.1/6.3/6.7, Corollaries6.4–6.6 and condition(D)"], "scope": "The original base is a complete discrete valuation ring. Its polyhedral correspondence gives components from vertices and orbit dimension complementary to face dimension, and condition(D) states regularity for unimodular simplices. The source omits the general proof of(D) and Proposition6.7. The corrected C2c proof independently gives the special integral fan, smooth charts and convergent complex-disc quotient with free properly discontinuous lattice action and compact fundamental-domain proof; analytic convergence is not attributed to a theorem stated only over the complete ring.", "reader": "GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, writing run; 17 November 2026 UTC"}]}], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#C2c", "terms_searched": ["semistable", "toric", "Mumford"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": "Mumford1972 section6 pp264–268 opened completely: polyhedral/orbit correspondence, lattice regularity condition and polarization proposition. The source works over a complete DVR, so the convergent analytic quotient is proved independently in the corrected block."}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Euler numbers in semistable toric rank-two models | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES:  | proof_sha256: 3e35cb18de8188ea402f957a74955ddb396f118e6beac3448fbf17f3fa57cace | remarks: Only zero-dimensional toric strata contribute, giving e=F. Counting incidences including self-identifications gives3F=2E and V-E+F=0, hence F=2V. The realization uses a positive integral convex height function, so this use is within the polarized Mumford construction. | remarks: Complete corrected block corrected_C2c_full_proof.tex retains Euler F=2V and supplies the smooth t=x1*x2*x3 charts, free lattice shear action, proper discontinuity and compact logarithmic fundamental-domain proof over an actual complex disc. Generic fibres are explicitly products C*/t^(NZ) times C*/t^Z. No formal-to-analytic theorem is used outside its hypothesis. | Credit evidence (cdp_audit/result_audit.json): Mumford1972 section6 pp264–268 opened completely: polyhedral/orbit correspondence, lattice regularity condition and polarization proposition. The source works over a complete DVR, so the convergent analytic quotient is proved independently in the corrected block. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_