eviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json.", "placement_revision": "Paper II owns the normal-crossing sign proof; Paper VI cites this statement", "pre_current_event_status": "historical record: Proved; current-writing proof review pending", "current_event_sources": ["records/sign_events.tsv"]}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C.2.NC.3", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C.2.NC.3", "source_file": "sections/part_C2_NC.tex; Statement C.2.NC.3", "source_line": 19294, "source_section": "Normal-crossing topology and canonical-flat component comparisons", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Uniform multiple normal-crossings fibres]\label{cdp:st:C.2.NC.3}
Let $g:Y\to C$ be a proper holomorphic map from a connected smooth compact complex threefold with $H^2(Y,\Q)=0$ to a smooth compact curve, with connected fibres and smooth general fibre of Euler characteristic zero. A fibre $mS$ with reduced normal-crossings support has
\[
 e(S)=\tau(S)\ge0.
 \tag{C.NC.8}\label{cdp:eq:C.NC.8}
\]
The normalized base change $t=s^m$ is finite étale of degree $m$ over a neighbourhood of $S$ and has reduced normal-crossings central fibre $S'$. Its possibly disconnected components do not affect the comparisons
$e(S')=m e(S)$ and $\tau(S')=m\tau(S)$.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normal.crossing", "multiplicit", "Euler"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.2.NC.3|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 30}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 35}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normal.crossing", "multiplicit", "Euler"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.2.NC.3|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 11}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normal.crossing", "multiplicit", "Euler"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.2.NC.3|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 19}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#C.2.NC.3", "terms_searched": ["normal.crossing", "multiplicit", "Euler"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Uniform multiple normal-crossings fibres | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: See records/A_notes.md for exact scope and verification. | remarks: After t=s^m the local normalization is w^m=u, s=w product(z_i), a finite etale degree-m cover of the support, possibly disconnected. Euler and triple count both multiply by m. No connectedness of this root cover is presumed. | proof_sha256: 7a41ea168e4fa575bd73f9273d078c07ded50fdc0ce0e2d0597fef3303573f0b | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json.", "placement_revision": "Paper II owns the normal-crossing sign proof; Paper VI cites this statement", "pre_current_event_status": "historical record: Proved; current-writing proof review pending", "current_event_sources": ["records/sign_events.tsv"]}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C.2.NC.4", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C.2.NC.4", "source_file": "sections/part_C2_NC.tex; Statement C.2.NC.4", "source_line": 19325, "source_section": "Normal-crossing topology and canonical-flat component comparisons", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Reducible normal-crossings fibres with unequal multiplicities]\label{cdp:st:C.2.NC.4}
Under the hypotheses on $g:Y\to C$ in \ref{cdp:st:C.2.NC.3}, let a fibre be $\sum_i m_iS_i$ with connected reducible normal-crossings support $S$. Its multiplicities may be unequal. Then
\[
 \tau(S)=0,\qquad e(S)=0.
 \tag{C.NC.9}\label{cdp:eq:C.NC.9}
\]
Every normalized conductor is a disjoint union of smooth elliptic curves, and every normalization component has Euler number zero. More generally, any singular normal-crossings fibre support under these hypotheses has either no triple point or exactly two triple points; in the latter case it is irreducible and its normalization is rational.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normal.crossing", "multiplicit", "Euler"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.2.NC.4|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 30}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 35}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normal.crossing", "multiplicit", "Euler"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.2.NC.4|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 11}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normal.crossing", "multiplicit", "Euler"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.2.NC.4|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "source