g up preserves coherent Euler and adds one to topological Euler. This supplies the stated numerical branches, not a proof of the full Enriques–Kodaira classification.", "reader": "GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, writing run; 17 November 2026 UTC"}]}], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#C.2.NC.4", "terms_searched": ["normal.crossing", "multiplicit", "Euler"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": "Original Peters table and BMS minimal odd-b1 elliptic Euler-zero assertion opened and matched."}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Reducible normal-crossings fibres with unequal multiplicities | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: See records/A_notes.md for exact scope and verification. | remarks: A rational normalization cannot meet a distinct global component: its pulled-back divisor line has rational Chern class zero and is actually trivial on the rational surface, contradicting its nonempty effective zero divisor. Thus a reducible support has no rational normalization; all remaining normalizations have chi(O)=0 and e>=0, forcing tau=e(S)=0. BMS statements about all Hopf fundamental groups being cyclic are not used. | proof_sha256: 1cc120299347e3cfc612ca6ed08c77aa72ac60fbc5b20d9c8506f91709d6802f | Credit evidence (cdp_audit/result_audit.json): Original Peters table and BMS minimal odd-b1 elliptic Euler-zero assertion opened and matched. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json