{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C2d", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C2d", "source_file": "sections/part_C2_jets.tex; Statement C2d", "source_line": 19534, "source_section": "Normal-crossing topology and canonical-flat component comparisons", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[The normal jets along cusp, tacnode and triple curves]\label{cdp:st:C2d}
Let $Y$ be a smooth complex threefold with $b_2(Y)=0$, let $S$ be a reduced Cartier divisor, and let $D\subset\operatorname{Sing}S$ be a smooth compact connected curve. Suppose the general plane section transverse to $D$ has one of the equations
\[
 x^2-y^3=0,\qquad x^2-y^4=0,\qquad xy(x-y)=0.
 \tag{C.J.1}\label{cdp:eq:C.J.1}
\]
Then $g(D)\le1$. For $g(D)=1$, the indicated transverse analytic type is constant along all of $D$. The inverse image of $D$ in the normalization is respectively an isomorphic copy, a finite etale cover of degree two, or a finite etale cover of degree three. Each connected component $C$ of that cover has genus one and normal line of degree zero in the normalization, which is smooth near $C$. At these three transverse types, the inverse Jacobian ideal pulls back into the line allowing at most a simple pole on each normalization branch.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normal.jet", "tacnod", "ordinary.triple"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C2d|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 0}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normal.jet", "tacnod", "ordinary.triple"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C2d|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 1}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normal.jet", "tacnod", "ordinary.triple"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C2d|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#C2d", "terms_searched": ["normal.jet", "tacnod", "ordinary.triple"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: The normal jets along cusp, tacnode and triple curves | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES:  | proof_sha256: c379133c0f0581df86b99a41e7d2f58feabdf694e48e1c89afe79681e665eaff | remarks: Cusp radical cubic and tacnode ac-b^2/4 have the stated intrinsic weights, including at quadratic zeros. The ordinary triple discriminant has degree4 and determinant weight6. Genus one makes all relevant sections nowhere zero and permits parameter-dependent normal forms; all branch covers are etale and normal lines have degree zero. Double-pole coefficient constraints annihilate every putative leading coefficient in the tacnode and triple cases. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json.", "placement_revision": "Paper II owns the normal-jet genus bound used in C4e/f and the irreducible sign proof.", "pre_current_event_status": "historical record: Proved; current-writing proof review pending", "current_event_sources": ["records/sign_events.tsv"]}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C.2.UN.1", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C.2.UN.1", "source_file": "sections/part_C2_unrestricted.tex; Statement C.2.UN.1", "source_line": 7504, "source_section": "Unrestricted Euler topology and component covers", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Every torus-degeneration fibre has even Euler number]\label{cdp:st:C.2.UN.1}
Let $f:Y\to B$ be a proper holomorphic map from a smooth complex
threefold to a smooth complex curve, with connected fibres and smooth
general fibre a complex two-torus. For every $b\in B$,
\[
                    e((Y_b)_{\rm red})\in2\Z.       \tag{C.UN.1}\label{cdp:eq:C.UN.1}
\]
This assertion allows arbitrary multiplicities and singularities and
imposes no K\"ahler or Betti-number hypothesis on $Y$.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["Euler", "generation", "torus"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.2.UN.1|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 83}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 100}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["Euler", "generation", "torus"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.2.UN.1|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 26}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["Euler", "generation", "torus"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C.2.UN.1|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_G