{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C4b", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C4b", "source_file": "sections/part_C4.tex; Statement C4b", "source_line": 45006, "source_section": "Global CDP replacement and normalization resonance", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[An unavoidable failure on a rational homology six-sphere]\label{cdp:st:C4b}
Let $f:Y\to\PP^1$ be a connected-fibre holomorphic map from a compact complex threefold with $b_1=b_2=b_3=0$. For every $L\in\Pic(Y)$ there is a scheme-theoretic fibre $F$ with
\[
 H^2(F,(T_Y\otimes L)|_F)\ne0,\qquad
 H^0(F,\Omega_Y^1|_F\otimes(K_Y\otimes L^{-1})|_F)\ne0. \tag{C.16}\label{cdp:eq:C.16}
\]
For torus general fibre the reduced fibre Euler numbers sum to two. Within the fibre class of \ref{cdp:st:C4a}, exactly one fibre has rational normalization; it is an irreducible reduced normal-crossing fibre of Euler number two. For that normalization,
\[
H^2(\widetilde S,K_{\widetilde S}\otimes
             \eta^*(K_Y^{-1}\otimes L))=\C
\quad\hbox{for every }L\in\Pic(Y).                    \tag{C.17}\label{cdp:eq:C.17}
\]
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["rational.homology", "six.sphere", "nonvanish"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C4b|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 3}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 3}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["rational.homology", "six.sphere", "nonvanish"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C4b|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 2}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["rational.homology", "six.sphere", "nonvanish"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C4b|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 16}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#C4b", "terms_searched": ["rational.homology", "six.sphere", "nonvanish"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: An unavoidable failure on a rational homology six-sphere | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES:  | proof_sha256: c726c9173143fe4598d7430a0905b3686576214c11289048c9b9c87f3e3c8e6a | remarks: Under b3=0 the all-twist H2 lower bound forces nonzero top cohomology on a full fibre. The normal-crossing classification isolates the rational normalization, whose torsion-free H2 and H1(O)=0 make every ambient line trivial there. Its canonical H2 is C by Serre duality. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json.", "pre_current_event_status": "historical record: Proved; current-writing proof review pending", "current_event_sources": ["records/sign_events.tsv"]}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C4e", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C4e", "source_file": "sections/part_C4.tex; Statement C4e", "source_line": 45115, "source_section": "Global CDP replacement and normalization resonance", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[The unrestricted normalization target under the integral CDP hypotheses]\label{cdp:st:C4e}
Let $f:Y\to\PP^1$ satisfy the integral CDP hypotheses and $c_3(Y)>0$. Then a fixed irreducible nonnormal reduced support $S$ has normalization $\eta:\widetilde S\to S$ satisfying
\[
 H^2\bigl(\widetilde S,\omega_{\widetilde S}\otimes
           \eta^*(K_Y^{-1}\otimes L)\bigr)\ne0
 \qquad\hbox{for every }L\in\Pic(Y).                  \tag{C.21}\label{cdp:eq:C.21}
\]
The assertion concerns the reduced support; no multiplicity-one conclusion is included.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normalisation", "Picard", "all.twist"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C4e|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 27}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 28}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normalisation", "Picard", "all.twist"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C4e|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["normalisation", "Picard", "all.twist"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C4e|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 13}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#C4e", "terms_searched": ["normalisation", "Picard", "all.twist"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Unrestricted all-twist normalization target under all integral CDP hypotheses | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: All general-fibre types; arbitrary conductor schemes and singularities. The target concerns a reduced support; no multiplicity-one assertion. | proof_sha256: b30c1b7fec8302a7cc6a3fb4050d906f3a22c1b4fe233ad934416bc1f917923f | remarks: Fixed-layer persistence is obtained before translating the ambient twist. The reduced-horizontal conductor case tracks the blowdown coefficient a=d-1, excludes new vertical conductor components on reversal, and uses codimension-one normal crossings plus the Jacobian-conductor criterion in codimension two. The doubled-horizontal case checks all conductor-exponent-two plane branches, the elliptic image, C2d constant type, normal degree zero and minimality. The simple-pole kernel lies in O(C) times the ambient line; its ruling pushforward admits sections for at most two degree-zero twists, so a connected persistent Picard image must be zero. The ten A5 prerequisites have a separate complete independent audit, merged below. No finite symbolic program is substituted for this geometric proof. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json.", "pre_current_event_status": "historical record: Proved; current-writing proof review pending", "current_event_sources": ["records/sign_events.tsv"]}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:C5b", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:C5b", "source_file": "sections/part_C5.tex; Statement C5b", "source_line": 45480, "source_section": "Global CDP replacement and normalization resonance", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Integral twists and the normalization-map exception]\label{cdp:st:C5b}
For $n\in\Z$ define
\[
 r_1(n)\equiv n\pmod3,\quad 0\le r_1(n)<3,
 \qquad r_2(n)\equiv3n\pmod4,\quad0\le r_2(n)<4,
\]
\begin{gather*}
 d(n)=\frac{n-4r_1(n)-3r_2(n)}{12},\qquad
 \epsilon_n=\begin{cases}0&3\mid n,\\1&3\nmid n.\end{cases}
\\
 u(n)=\max\{d(n)+1,0\},\qquad
 v(n)=\max\{-d(n)-1,0\}.
\end{gather*}
The coarse direct images of $T_X\otimes M_n$ are
\begin{align*}
 f_*(T_X\otimes M_n)&=\OO(d(n))\oplus\OO(d(n-1)),\\
 R^1f_*(T_X\otimes M_n)&=\OO(d(n))\oplus\OO(d(n-1))\oplus\OO(d(n+2)),\\
 R^2f_*(T_X\otimes M_n)&=\OO(d(n+6))\oplus\C_{p_1}^{\epsilon_n}.\tag{C.5}\label{cdp:eq:C.5}
\end{align*}
Their global cohomology dimensions are
\begin{align*}
 h^0&=u(n)+u(n-1),\\
 h^1&=v(n)+v(n-1)+u(n)+u(n-1)+u(n+2),\\
 h^2&=v(n)+v(n-1)+v(n+2)+u(n+6)+\epsilon_n,\\
 h^3&=v(n+6).                                             \tag{C.6}\label{cdp:eq:C.6}
\end{align*}
The natural map $H^2(X,T_X\otimes M_n)\to H^2(\mathrm dP_6,K_{\mathrm dP_6})=\C$ has rank one exactly for
\[
 n\in\{-6,-3,-2\}\cup\Z_{\ge0};                         \tag{C.7}\label{cdp:eq:C.7}
\]
it is zero for all other integers. In particular $M_{-1}$ has tangent cohomology $(0,0,1,0)$ and a zero map to the normalization target.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["integral.twist", "normalisation", "exception"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C5b|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 28}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 29}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["integral.twist", "normalisation", "exception"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C5b|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["integral.twist", "normalisation", "exception"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#C5b|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 62}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#C5b", "terms_searched": ["integral.twist", "normalisation", "exception"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Integral twists and the normalization-map exception | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES:  | proof_sha256: 67aca7b9de601dd05557a9907f56cf7ddd2c4449533f21d16cea2c4126e2e0a6 | remarks: Checked the normalized Kodaira–Spencer matrix [[0,y],[y,x]], both connecting maps, length-two root skyscraper, cusp elementary modification and R2(T)=O(6) plus Q. Checked all integer residue classes and actual map rank: surjective exactly for n in {-6,-3,-2} or n>=0. The n=-1 example has tangent cohomology (0,0,1,0) but normalization map zero. The program checks 481 bounded weighted comparisons; the general weighted monomial count and all-stalk analytic argument were read separately. This overlaps INV D computations but preserves the distinct exact normalization-map exception. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json.", "pre_current_event_status": "historical record: Proved; current-writing proof review pending", "current_event_sources": ["records/sign_events.tsv"]}

