lines930–1108; only the opened portion of case(ii) is within this additional reading", "Theorem6.1 p19 onward: source lines1502–1618, hexagonal setup and displayed independent logarithmic period/action formulas; this is a partial proof reading", "Numbered locators verified by compiling unchanged supplied source: t:main=Theorem1.1 p1; degrees=Theorem3.2 p8; smoothingbound=section9.2 p30"], "scope": "The actual supplied source was opened and its stated hypotheses matched, including m>=12, unchanged singular-fibre types and fixed limiting periods. It establishes det degree2m-1, nonnegative splitting, h(O) and a section-family lower bound8m-8. It does not establish the later exact tangent dimensions or smooth miniversal8m+1 germ; those require the separate complete E15 proof. No independent online metadata verification is claimed. The exact printed Theorem2.2 is the whole conclusion of E4, whose full proof is a re-derivation; the source acknowledges a Gabber outline through Conrad and its analytic Raynaud counterpart. Theorem2.3 contains the torus/S6 cup-product argument extended by D1.12. Theorem4.1 case(i) and the opened rank-two local formulas give logarithmic coefficient I at the retained hexagonal cusp. This additional event does not claim a complete reading of the whole Theorem6.1 proof.", "reader": "GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, writing run; 17 November 2026 UTC"}]}], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#E4", "terms_searched": ["local.freeness", "locally.free", "Proposition 5.1"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: R1g_*O locally free for proper connected maps from smooth manifolds to curves | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: Cyclic normalization and finite invariants include multiple fibres. | proof_sha256: e566426b39c14b46185b08b52eb3c920812d91e346bc7580524b43e38415b544 | remarks: The common-multiplicity root cover has normal local components given by finite diagonal quotients of polydiscs, and averaging identifies the reduced parameter quotient. The normalized cover need not be connected locally; global connectedness follows from the smooth connected general fibre. Invariants recover the original resolved normal total space. R1 of the original map injects into the locally free invariant direct image, so it is torsion-free and locally free on the curve. Parameter multiplication then gives H0(O_full fibre)=C. No Grauert–Riemenschneider vanishing is invoked. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json."}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:E10", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:E10", "source_file": "sections/part_E.tex; Statement E10", "source_line": 47128, "source_section": "Fibration stability and explicit deformation calculations", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Counterexample", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Counterexample: A fixed positive-genus target in the unrestricted stability assertion]\label{cdp:st:E10}
The assertion that every small deformation of a fibration extends
over its original fixed positive-genus target curve $C$ is false even for a torus
fibration with Kodaira--Spencer rank two at a regular value.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["positive.genus", "fixed.target", "Kodaira.Spencer"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#E10|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 0}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["positive.genus", "fixed.target", "Kodaira.Spencer"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#E10|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["positive.genus", "fixed.target", "Kodaira.Spencer"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#E10|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#E10", "terms_searched": ["positive.genus", "fixed.target", "Kodaira.Spencer"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Fixed positive-genus-target stability fails even with rank-two torus KS | SOURCE STATUS: Refuted | SOURCE NOTES: Explicit Hesse-product/genus-two deformation. P1 replacement proved in E6. | proof_sha256: 5bc2adefb92a02c02576fa659ffee3dc1f9a106e913c61076824d6fbab62b9ad | remarks: The disjoint Hesse critical sets keep the fibre product smooth. Moving one of six branch values while five are fixed gives nonzero base Kodaira–Spencer class. Leray gives h(O)=(1,2,6,5), h(g*TC)=(0,3,10,7), h(Trelative)=(0,6,20,14); the nonzero class lands injectively in H1(g*TC). This refutes extension to an arbitrary fixed positive-genus target, not E6 over P1. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | Final II source-to-print retention: complete normalized canonical blocks retained; exact mathematical/citation changes separately reviewed in records/II_editorial_mathematical_changes.json, II_working_supplement_root_changes.json and II_positive_credit_changes.json."}

{"row_key": "S6_03_CDP:E16", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "cdp:st:E16", "source_file": "sections/part_E_rank.tex; Statement E16", "source_line": 48146, "source_section": "Fibration stability and explicit deformation calculations", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Rank divisors from the root Kodaira--Spencer morphism]\label{cdp:st:E16}
We use the logarithmic Kodaira--Spencer morphism at the specified degenerate fibres and the ordinary morphism on the finite smooth torus covers. For the original affine-twist family, including every $|p|>1$, its only rank defect is rank one at the order-three point. The logarithmic cusp has rank two. For the $(3k,4l)$ logarithmic transforms, on their full root covers the ranks at the two multiple values are respectively
\[
 \begin{cases}1&k=1,\\0&k>1,\end{cases}
 \qquad
 \begin{cases}2&l=1,\\0&l>1.\end{cases}                 \tag{E.16.1}\label{cdp:eq:E.16.1}
\]
Every other smooth point and the logarithmic cusp have rank two.

For the two-parameter family the logarithmic rank is one at each of its two rank-one nodal values, zero at the order-four root point, and two everywhere else, including the hexagonal fibre. Its determinant has simple coarse zeros at the two nodal values and order four in the root coordinate at the multiple value. For the Liu--Rollenske central family the logarithmic rank is two at both the cuspidal and hexagonal fibres and throughout the remaining smooth locus; at the order-four root point it is zero, and its determinant has order four there.

For a specified positive comb section $\sigma$ of degree parameter $m$, let $x,y$ be root coordinates of weights $3,4$, with $y=0$ at the order-three point. There is a nonzero homogeneous polynomial $P_\sigma(X,Y)$ of degree $4m$, uniquely determined up to an overall nonzero scalar by the marked period section, such that
\[
 \det\kappa_\sigma=y^2P_\sigma(x^4,y^3).             \tag{E.16.2}\label{cdp:eq:E.16.2}
\]
The rank-defect set is exactly its zero divisor. At any such point the rank is zero exactly when all four entries of the actual Kodaira--Spencer matrix vanish; otherwise it is one. Formula \eqref{cdp:eq:E.16.3} below computes those entries from $\sigma$. No unspecified choice of a comb section is assigned a fixed root set. The polynomial is nonzero at the hexagonal cusp, so that cusp always has rank two.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["rank.divisor", "Kodaira.Spencer", "theta"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#E16|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex", "sha256": "9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170", "hit_count": 106}, {"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 1}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["rank.divisor", "Kodaira.Spencer", "theta"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#E16|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 18}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["rank.divisor", "Kodaira.Spencer", "theta"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_searches_239.json#E16|DGKX_v1", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2610.00250v1_Du_Guo_Kusakabe_Xie_src/v5oka_maps_modifications_deformations.tex", "sha256": "924a4a72d80793927f3104121a44786ea2b9869ae6ea2bca5a6a69553ab2884e", "hit_count": 30}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_context_readings.json#DGKX_v1", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified within the listed queries and actually read contexts. Related construction data or general lemmas may occur; the saved hit list is not a claim that every hit was read."}", "found_elsewhere": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "full_statement_found": false, "matches": [], "cited_opened_inputs": [], "additional_attached_search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/credit_elsewhere_searches_239.json#E16", "terms_searched": ["rank.divisor", "Kodaira.Spencer", "theta"], "corpus_size_files": 43, "bounded_absence_statement": "Beyond the explicit positive matches and opened general inputs, no full counterpart was identified in the executed attached-source searches and stated context readings. This is not an exhaustive priority search of all literature.", "existing_scoped_credit_notes": ""}"}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Exact Kodaira-Spencer rank divisors in every specified family | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: Comb divisor y^2 P_sigma(x^4,y^3), with degree(P_sigma)=4m and explicit Gauss-Manin Wronskian. | proof_sha256: 4ef3109c6082d9796df1610fcf7d8a3fa94b724cbddba391fa860db6e7d6ec91 | remarks: Higher root transforms multiply the ordinary tensor by k*u^(k-1) or l*u^(l-1). For P(1,4), weighted entry orders force the root zero; the degree budget forces the stated exact nodal orders. For a specified comb, det(kappa)=y^2 P_sigma(x^4,y^3) with degree(P_sigma)=4m; no fixed defect set is assigned to an unspecified section. Source E16 has a typographic malformed text command in(E.16.3), to correct in the printed version. | Explicit source comparison: work/cdp_audit/credit_comparison_239.json | F