{"row_key": "S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS:B.1.2", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "maps:src:B.1.2", "source_file": "sections/maps.tex, Theorem B.1.2", "source_line": 391, "source_section": "Sphere maps, framings and homotopy classes", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Theorem", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}\label{maps:src:B.1.2}

For the repaired quotient of Paper~I, Theorem~17.4 with $|p|=1$,
\[
 [e]=6\nu'=\eta_3\eta_4\eta_5\ne0
       \quad\text{in }\pi_6(S^3)=\mathbb Z/12.
 \tag{B.1.1}\label{maps:eq:B.1.1}
\]
Its stable class is $12\nu$ and its real Adams invariant
is $1/2\in\mathbb Q/\mathbb Z$.

