{"row_key": "S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS:B.6.9", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "maps:src:B.6.9", "source_file": "sections/maps.tex, Proposition B.6.9", "source_line": 41239, "source_section": "Known source results and complete re-derivations", "placement_basis": "inventory kind and plan condition 2", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Cited/re-derived", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Credited re-derivation: a complex filling is sufficient]\label{maps:src:B.6.9}

Let $M_r$ be the oriented mapping torus for $r$ positive parameter
loops, either before or after the conifold surgery, and suppose
that a compact almost complex eight-manifold $V$ has boundary
identified orientation-preservingly with $M_r$. Then
\[
 r a=\frac{-c_1(V)^4+4c_1(V)^2c_2(V)+3c_2(V)^2
                    -3\operatorname{sign}(V)}{24}
       \quad\hbox{in }\mathbb Z/28.
 \tag{B.6.18}\label{maps:eq:B.6.18}
\]
All characteristic products are evaluated using relative lifts;
their boundary restrictions vanish. A spin condition on $V$ is
unnecessary. The formula is conditional on the actual boundary
identification and on the indicated characteristic numbers;
no such filling or numerical value is inferred from it.

\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "Only homotopy-sphere/h-cobordism background is located in the inspected hits; no displayed spin-c filling formula for this return.", "found_in_E26": "Only the smooth six-sphere recognition/h-cobordism background is located; no displayed spin-c return formula.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "Inspected coboundary hits are affine group cocycles, not the eight-dimensional spin-c characteristic formula.", "found_elsewhere": "Known characteristic formula: Crowley–Nordstrom spin-c coboundary formula, published2021 Lemma2.1/equation(2.1), rewritten using p1=c1²−2c2. The manuscript correctly labels this Known."}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: Any correctly bounded almost complex eight-manifold evaluates rPhi by (-c1^4+4c1^2c2+3c2^2-3signature)/24 modulo28; a spin filling is unnecessary. | SOURCE STATUS: Known | SOURCE NOTES: This is a conditional filling formula. The actual free-circle filling and spin trace in B.6.15-B.6.24 subsequently give the numerical residue zero for every requested family. | Separate DGKXv2 comparison: No spin-c filling formula located by the recorded terms. | Final bounded source comparison: work/maps_audit/maps60_credit_comparison.json | source_blocks: [{"id": "B.6.9", "file": "sources/returns/S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS/sections/maps_B.tex", "start_line": 1988, "end_line": 2038, "source_sha256": "937cc1db8de60d8f9a8c4cd792f660569ea7af15f1665c5ea1e4848c1713d693"}] | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_maps60_final_closure.json | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json"}

{"row_key": "S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS:B.6.25", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "maps:src:B.6.25", "source_file": "sections/maps.tex, Corollary B.6.25", "source_line": 4462, "source_section": "Sphere maps, framings and homotopy classes", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Corollary", "source_statement": "\begin{corollary}[an explicit spin filling after the computation]\label{maps:src:B.6.25}

Every mapping torus in \ref{maps:src:B.6.24} has a spin eight-manifold
filling diffeomorphic to $D^7\times S^1$, with one
zero-handle and one one-handle, and with
$p_1^2=\operatorname{sign}=0$.
\end{corollary}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "AC26 base-fibre mapping-torus/isotopy facts concern geometric monodromy of the torus fibration. They do not compute the parameter-circle class in Theta7.", "found_in_E26": "E26 supplies the sphere family but no parameter-circle Theta7 value is identified in the inspected scope.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "DGKX v1 even-shift biholomorphisms and exact affine closing supply the actual gluing antecedent; they do not themselves evaluate its smooth Theta7 class.", "found_elsewhere": "Elementary D7×S1 filling after an actual isotopy has been proved; its zero Pontryagin square/signature do not supply a new independent monodromy proof."}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: After the computed zero monodromy, every requested mapping torus has an explicit spin filling D7xS1 with one zero-handle and one one-handle and p1-square=signature=0. | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: This filling is constructed after the numerical computation, not assumed to prove it. Product orientation is D7 thenS1; both boundary spin structures extend. | Separate DGKXv2 comparison: DGKX v2 gives the underlying source model but no parameter-circle Theta7 evaluation identified. | Final bounded source comparison: work/maps_audit/maps60_credit_comparison.json | source_blocks: [{"id": "B.6.25", "file": "sources/returns/S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS/sections/maps_B.tex", "start_line": 3190, "end_line": 3216, "source_sha256": "937cc1db8de60d8f9a8c4cd792f660569ea7af15f1665c5ea1e4848c1713d693"}] | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_maps60_final_closure.json | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json"}

{"row_key": "S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS:D.2.17", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "maps:src:D.2.17", "source_file": "sections/manifolds.tex", "source_line": 8389, "source_section": "The other six-manifolds", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Corollary", "source_statement": "\begin{corollary}[two further original additive profiles]\label{maps:src:D.2.17}

