\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "No four-dimensional complex construction or rank-three Kuhn specialization theorem identified by the recorded terms; the rank-two source construction is prior input.", "found_in_E26": "The elliptic surface and its global Weierstrass model are prior input. No full fourfold/Kuhn-cusp integral-specialization assertion identified.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "The fibre-product hits concern lower-dimensional local models/base changes, not this compact complex fourfold or its integral homology.", "found_elsewhere": "A direct local invariant-ring counterexample to the literal normalization assertion; no independent full matching refutation identified in the bounded sources."}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: The literal normalization in Lead 6 is not the asserted good-reduction quotient. | SOURCE STATUS: Refuted | SOURCE NOTES: Normalization cannot contract the IV* or III components. | audit_notes: Scoped progress, not a complete-chain certification. F.3.11 gives bounded correction at one retained cusp; it does not establish simultaneous good reduction at every finite puncture. | Separate DGKXv2 comparison: The fibre-product hits concern local/base-change constructions, not this compact complex fourfold or its integral homology. | Final bounded source comparison: work/maps_audit/maps60_credit_comparison.json | source_blocks: [{"id": "E.1.1", "file": "sources/returns/S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS/sections/fourfolds.tex", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 36, "source_sha256": "19ceb389423e80bf1e63e8ac36718a2b26c59e2fa0e033462604af5416ec24c7"}] | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_maps60_final_closure.json | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json"}

{"row_key": "S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS:E.1.3", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "maps:src:E.1.3", "source_file": "sections/fourfolds.tex: E.1.3", "source_line": 19786, "source_section": "The fourfold and transverse fibre products", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Theorem", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}[the integral cusp calculation]\label{maps:src:E.1.3}

For the central fibre $W_3$ of \eqref{maps:eq:E.5},
\[
 H_q(W_3;\mathbb Z)=\mathbb Z^{b_q},\qquad
 (b_0,\ldots,b_6)=(1,3,9,9,10,3,1).
 \tag{E.6}\label{maps:eq:E.6}
\]
Integral specialization is onto the monodromy invariant lattice in
every degree.  Its only kernel is a copy of $\mathbb Z$ in degree four.

\end{theorem}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "No four-dimensional complex construction or rank-three Kuhn specialization theorem identified by the recorded terms; the rank-two source construction is prior input.", "found_in_E26": "The elliptic surface and its global Weierstrass model are prior input. No full fourfold/Kuhn-cusp integral-specialization assertion identified.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "The fibre-product hits concern lower-dimensional local models/base changes, not this compact complex fourfold or its integral homology.", "found_elsewhere": "Chen2021 ThB gives the rational local invariant-cycle input under the exact Kähler/proper/SNC hypotheses; Deligne HodgeIII proper simplicial weights and the fully printed cellular calculation prove the stated free integral specialization. Rational invariant cycles alone do not imply integral saturation."}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: The rank-three cusp has free homology (1,3,9,9,10,3,1); integral specialization is onto the invariant lattices with kernel Z only in degree four. | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: Exact normalization matrices; toric line-bundle descent; integral exterior-generator Smith forms. | audit_notes: Scoped progress, not a complete-chain certification. F.3.11 gives bounded correction at one retained cusp; it does not establish simultaneous good reduction at every finite puncture. | Separate DGKXv2 comparison: The fibre-product hits concern local/base-change constructions, not this compact complex fourfold or its integral homology. | Final bounded source comparison: work/maps_audit/maps60_credit_comparison.json | source_blocks: [{"id": "E.1.3", "file": "sources/returns/S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS/sections/fourfolds.tex", "start_line": 159, "end_line": 293, "source_sha256": "19ceb389423e80bf1e63e8ac36718a2b26c59e2fa0e033462604af5416ec24c7"}] | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_maps60_final_closure.json | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json"}

{"row_key": "S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS:F.1.4", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "maps:src:F.1.4", "source_file": "sections/fourfolds.tex: F.1.4", "source_line": 24475, "source_section": "The rank-three search and a parity obstruction", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[the diagonal obstruction]\label{maps:src:F.1.4}

If $A\in\operatorname{GL}_n(\mathbb Z)$ has no eigenvalue one,
every affine map $x\mapsto Ax+b$ of $\mathbb R^n/\mathbb Z^n$
has a fixed point.  Thus the diagonal elliptic finite monodromies
in Lead 7 admit no free affine lifts.

\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "The source square-zero unipotent cusp is a lower-rank example; it does not state the general primitive rank-three normal form/centralizer or the affine fixed-point obstruction.", "found_in_E26": "No full statement of either rank-six linear assertion located by the recorded terms.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "DGKX v1 AppendixC has the original rank-four common centralizer and period-shift calculation. This is a related lower-rank calculation, not the displayed primitive rank-three block centralizer or affine fixed-point theorem.", "found_elsewhere": "Elementary affine linear algebra: invertibility of I−A solves the fixed-point equation. This is a classical obstruction, applied to refute the proposed diagonal tuple."}, "historical_source_notes": "SOURCE STATEMENT: A finite linear map without eigenvalue one admits no fixed-point-free affine lift; hence the diagonal candidate fails. | SOURCE STATUS: Proved | SOURCE NOTES: Solve (I-A)x=v over R. | audit_notes: Scoped progress, not a complete-chain certification. F.3.11 gives bounded correction at one retained cusp; it does not establish simultaneous good reduction at every finite puncture. | Separate DGKXv2 comparison: DGKX v2 free affine local cyclic action is related construction input, not either stated general linear-algebra assertion. | Final bounded source comparison: work/maps_audit/maps60_credit_comparison.json | source_blocks: [{"id": "F.1.4", "file": "sources/returns/S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS/sections/fourfolds.tex", "start_line": 744, "end_line": 756, "source_sha256": "19ceb389423e80bf1e63e8ac36718a2b26c59e2fa0e033462604af5416ec24c7"}] | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_maps60_final_closure.json | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json", "pre_current_event_status": "historical record: Proved; current-writing proof review pending", "current_event_sources": ["analysis/V/current_check_events.tsv"]}

{"row_key": "S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS:F.2.3", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "maps:src:F.2.3", "source_file": "sections/fourfolds.tex: F.2.3", "source_line": 24560, "source_section": "The rank-three search and a parity obstruction", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Counterexample", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Counterexample: determination by peripheral data alone]\label{maps:src:F.2.3}

Monodromy matrices and affine twist vectors alone do not
determine the homology of a compact glued manifold.  A cusp
filling, or an equivalent relative topological specification,
is additional data.

