{"row_key": "S6_04_MAPS_MANIFOLDS:F.2.36", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "maps:src:F.2.36", "source_file": "sections/fourfolds_integral_conjugacy.tex", "source_line": 29741, "source_section": "The rank-three search and a parity obstruction", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Theorem", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}[simultaneous integral conjugacy for every input]\label{maps:src:F.2.36}

There is an unconditional exact algorithm which decides simultaneous
$\mathrm{GL}_6(\mathbb Z)$ conjugacy of any two marked matrix tuples of
F.2 and returns a conjugating matrix when one exists. The algorithm
does not impose a bound on their entries, on the affine multiplicities,
or on the integral conjugator. More generally it applies to any integral
tuple containing a matrix $1+N$ with $N^2=0$ and $\operatorname{rank}N=3$;
the primitive-image assumption is unnecessary for this statement.

\end{theorem}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_scoped_comparison", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["simultaneous.*conjugacy", "principal.ideal", "Bley", "Hofmann", "Johnston"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_credit/searches_55.json#F.2.36|AC26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_credit/context_readings.json#AC26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified in the saved result-specific queries and the explicitly reviewed contexts. All hits remain available; this does not claim that every broad-word context or the entire external literature was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_scoped_comparison", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["simultaneous.*conjugacy", "principal.ideal", "Bley", "Hofmann", "Johnston"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_credit/searches_55.json#F.2.36|E26", "searched_files": [{"path": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "hit_count": 0}], "actual_reading_scope_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_credit/context_readings.json#E26", "matches": [], "relation": "No full matching receiving statement was identified in the saved result-specific queries and the explicitly reviewed contexts. All hits remain available; this does not claim that every broad-word context or the entire external literature was read."}", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "{"status": "not_found_in_scoped_comparison", "full_statement_found": false, "terms_searched": ["simultaneous.*conjugacy", "principal.ideal", "Bley", "Hofmann", "Johnston"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/maps_credit/searches_55.json#F.2.36|DGKX_v1", "se