{"row_key": "S6_05_ARITHMETIC:C.2.2", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "ari:C.2.2", "source_file": "C_special.tex C.2.2; code/Cspecial_reflection.out", "source_line": 5457, "source_section": "Special values, local expansions and torsion", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[the real locus]\label{ari:C.2.2}
An antiholomorphic equivalence $X_c\to X_{c'}$ exists exactly when
