{"row_key": "S6_05_ARITHMETIC:C.6.2", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "ari:C.6.2", "source_file": "sections/C_heights.tex C.6.2", "source_line": 6087, "source_section": "Global heights and the eleven rational CM fibres", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[exact finite local-height calculation]\label{ari:C.6.2}
Let $E/\Q$ be a global minimal Weierstrass model. If $mP$ is
in the identity component at $p$, and $mP\ne O$, then
\begin{equation}\label{ari:eq:ch-local-exact}
 \frac{\lambda_p(P)}{\log p}
 =\frac{v_p(\Delta)}{12}
   +\frac{\frac12\max(0,-v_p(x(mP)))-v_p(\psi_m(P))}{m^2}.
\end{equation}
For $m=1$ we read $\psi_1=1$. This formula, with exact rational
coordinates and valuations, gives all the finite contributions
