{"row_key": "S6_05_ARITHMETIC:C.8.1", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "ari:C.8.1", "source_file": "sections/C_analytic.tex C.8.1", "source_line": 7446, "source_section": "An analytic proof of the elliptic maximum", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[three uniform bounds on the elliptic norm]\label{ari:C.8.1}
For every $z\in\C$ and every $\tau$ in the standard modular
fundamental region, we have
\[
 \begin{array}{c|ccc}
 \text{restriction}&T\le2&T\le7/5&T\le11/10\\ \hline
 N(z,\tau)&<17/10&<3/2&<143/100.
 \end{array}
\]
If $\wp_\tau(z)=0$ and $T\ge2$, then $N(z,\tau)<541/500$.
