{"row_key": "S6_05_ARITHMETIC:C.8.3", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "ari:C.8.3", "source_file": "sections/C_analytic.tex C.8.3", "source_line": 7721, "source_section": "An analytic proof of the elliptic maximum", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[the comparison of the two local discs]\label{ari:C.8.3}
Every complex number $t_0$ with $|t_0-1|\le1/500$ has a
representative $\tau$ with $|\tau-i|<1/50$ and $j(\tau)=1728t_0$.
Consequently every zero of $\wp$ for that modulus satisfies
$N\le\sqrt2$, with equality only for $t_0=1$.
