{"row_key": "S6_05_ARITHMETIC:C.8.9", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "ari:C.8.9", "source_file": "sections/C_measure.tex C.8.9", "source_line": 8077, "source_section": "An analytic proof of the elliptic maximum", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Correction", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Refuted sign and normalization, with the corrected current identity proved]\label{ari:C.8.9}
On a local period chart write $\mu=a\tau+b$, with $a,b$ real,
and put $T=\Im\tau$. The positive Betti measure is
\[
 m_P=db\wedge da
 =\frac{|\mu_w-a\tau_w|^2}{T}\,dA_w.
\]
Thus the proposed form $da\wedge db$ has the wrong sign.
The globally single-valued function $L(t)=\log N(P_t)$ satisfies
on $\mathbb P^1(\C)$
\begin{equation}\label{ari:eq:ca-current}
 dd^cL=\frac1{12}\delta_\infty-m_P,\qquad
               \int_{\mathbb P^1}m_P=\frac1{12}.
\end{equation}
There are no atoms of $m_P$ at $0$, $1$ or $\infty$.
Let $T_0=\sqrt3/2$, $\rho=(1+i\sqrt3)/2$, and
$p=\wp'_\rho((2-\rho)/3)$. The density in the ordinary
$t$ coordinate satisfies
\begin{align}
 \frac{dm_P}{dA_t}
 &=\frac{|t|^{-2/3}}{64T_0|p|^{2/3}}
                      \bigl(1+O(|t|^{1/3})\bigr),
                         &&t\longrightarrow0,\label{ari:eq:ca-density0}\\
 \frac{dm_P}{dA_t}
 &=\frac{|t-1|^{-3/2}}{24\pi^2\sqrt{E_4(i)}}
                      \bigl(1+O(|t-1|^{1/2})\bigr),
                         &&t\longrightarrow1.\label{ari:eq:ca-density1}
\end{align}
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "citation_key": "AC2026", "original_source": "sources/original/AC26_original_manuscript.pdf", "source_sha256": "283bba102dd1d5dc346af81b28145bdaaea6654398d5032e76e97bafb9a858f2", "actual_reading_scope": "Attached original PDF: Remark 1.3 p.5; Proposition 7.27 pp.62–63; Theorem 9.1 pp.64–65; Proposition 9.11 pp.70–71; Lemma 9.12 pp.71–74; Proposition 9.13 pp.74–75; Remark 9.21 p.81; Theorem 10.5 pp.88–89; Proposition 10.8 pp.92–94. Also original PDF Theorem 5.4(iii) p.32 and its flat-character proof p.35; Theorem 9.1(vi) p.65; Proposition 9.20 p.80; Corollary 9.22 p.81; Remark9.27 p.83. The original PDF, not the transcription, governs the comparison.", "search": {"record_file": "work/invariants_arithmetic/credit_search_log.json", "record_key": "S6_05_ARITHMETIC:C.8.9|AC26", "terms_searched": ["maximum", "critical", "Mahler", "Gaussian", "equidistribution", "duplication", "ray", "216"], "hit_counts": {"maximum": 4, "critical": 3, "Mahler": 0, "Gaussian": 0, "equidistribution": 0, "duplication": 0, "ray": 29, "216": 0}}, "full_statement_found": false, "kind": "bounded_negative", "locator": "", "relation": "The precise result was not found in the explicitly listed original-source sections and statement searches. This is not a claim of absence from unread sections or from the literature as a whole."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "not_found_in_checked_scope", "citation_key": "Engel2026", "original_source": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "source_sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36", "actual_reading_scope": "S6.tex §1 lines235–280; §2 lines288–390; main-thm lines882–910; integral homology lines1617–1643; remarks1647–1725.", "search": {"record_file": "work/invariants_arithmetic/credit_search_log.json", "record_key": "S6_05_ARITHMETIC:C.8.9|E26", "terms_searched": ["maximum", "critical", "Mahler", "Gaussia