{"row_key": "S6_05_ARITHMETIC:C.8.14", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "ari:C.8.14", "source_file": "sections/C_critical.tex", "source_line": 8452, "source_section": "Critical points and the global level curves", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[the compact exclusion by one Cayley disc]\label{ari:C.8.14}
Let $\chi=(\tau-i)/(\tau+i)$. On
$0<|\chi|\le2-\sqrt3$, the invariant $F$ satisfies $|F|<1$.
At the two equianharmonic points on the boundary its continuous
value is $3/4$.
