{"row_key": "WORKING_CDP:lem:conormal-injective", "source_compendium_paper": "II", "source_compendium_label": "wbII:lem:conormal-injective", "source_file": "workbench/cdp_program.tex", "source_line": 2580, "source_section": "Cotangent torsion, conductor and the printed endpoint error", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[The conormal filtration and its exact section criterion]\label{cdp:st:A.1.1}\label{wbII:prop:criterion}\label{wbII:prop:filtration}\label{wbII:lem:conormal}\label{wbII:lem:conormal-injective}\label{wbII:prop:missing-global-section-criterion}\label{wbII:prop:missing-cotangent-filtration}
The conormal map $d:N^*\to V$, defined by $[F]\mapsto dF|_S$ for a local defining equation $F$, is injective. With $K=\ker(V\to Q)$, there are canonical exact sequences
\begin{align}
0&\longrightarrow N^*\xrightarrow{d}K\longrightarrow T\longrightarrow0,
\label{cdp:A:filtration1}\\
0&\longrightarrow K\longrightarrow V\longrightarrow Q\longrightarrow0.
\label{cdp:A:filtration2}
\end{align}
Let $\partial_A:H^0(S,Q\otimes A)\to H^1(S,K\otimes A)$ and $\delta_A:H^0(S,T\otimes A)\to H^1(S,N^*\otimes A)$ be their connecting maps. Then
\[
 H^0(S,V\otimes A)=0
 \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
 H^0(S,K\otimes A)=0\ \hbox{and}\ \partial_A\hbox{ is injective}.
\tag{A.1}\label{cdp:eq:A.1}
\]
Under the explicit hypotheses $H^0(S,N^*\otimes A)=0$ and $H^0(S,Q\otimes A)=0$, $H^0(S,V\otimes A)$ is canonically $\ker\delta_A$.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status":"found_matching_known_conclusion_in_specified_scope","full_statement_or_conclusion_found":true,"comparison":"The original source uses the xy and xyz normal-crossing local models and proves injectivity of h maps to h dg. This is the same NC statement, although the receiving canonical A.1.1 also treats general reduced Cartier divisors.","positive_or_context_locator":"Setup10.1 and equation(10.1), p.86","terms_searched":["conormal","nonzerodivisor","normal crossings"],"searched_files":[{"path":"sources/original/AC26_transcription.tex","sha256":"9e87e12175c70040ed66ab6513172a1f952c96205601c0910f48712c42445170"},{"path":"sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt","sha256":"e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040"}],"search_record":"deliverables/work/cdp_audit/II_working_credit/searches_150.json#lem:conormal-injective|AC26","full_search_hits":"deliverables/work/cdp_audit/II_working_credit/search_hits/lem_conormal-injective__AC26.txt","actual_context_readings":"deliverables/work/cdp_audit/II_working_credit/context_readings.json#AC26","negative_search_limit":"A bounded search and the listed opened contexts do not establish absence from all literature or that every unrelated hit was read."}", "found_in_E26": "{"status":"full_counterpart_not_identified_in_bounded_checked_scope","full_statement_or_conclusion_found":false,"comparison":"No full counterpart to this exact receiving statement was identified in the per-row queries and opened Engel contexts. The construction and invariant-form discussion is not equated with a conductor, duality, or coherent vanishing theorem.","positive_or_context_locator":"Opened §6 invariant-form context and final comparison; see context_readings.json#E26","terms_searched":["conormal","nonzerodivisor","normal crossings"],"searched_files":[{"path":"sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex","sha256":"95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef