{"row_key": "working_edition:cusp-cone-native-descent", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "wb:cusp-cone-native-descent", "source_file": "sources/workbench/cusp_cone_sphere_routes.tex", "source_line": 36366, "source_section": "Local covers, global quotients and cusp carriers", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Lemma", "source_statement": "\begin{lemma}[The native quotient over the whole punctured cusp]
\label{wb:cusp-cone-native-descent}
There is a well-defined real-analytic fibrewise group epimorphism
\begin{equation}
 \overline\pi:N_0\setminus W
 \longrightarrow D_0^*\times\overline T^2
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-native-family-map}
\end{equation}
whose kernel is the connected two-torus family defined by \(K_\Lambda\).
The target local system is trivial.  On the positive radial fibre \(F_T\),
\(t=e^{-2\pi T}\), the isomorphism
\begin{equation}
 \iota_T:\overline T^2\longrightarrow Q_T,\qquad
 [(a,b)]\longmapsto[Y_T(a,b)^{\mathsf T}]
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-radial-isometry}
\end{equation}
satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \pi_T=\iota_T\circ\overline\pi|_{F_T}.
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-native-restriction}
\end{equation}
If \(\overline T^2\) is given the pullback by \(\iota_T\) of the
Euclidean quotient metric on \(Q_T=\mathbb R^2/Y_T\mathbb Z^2\), then
\(\iota_T\) is an isometry and
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{sys}(\overline T^2,g_T)
 =\operatorname{sys}(Q_T)\geq T-C.
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-native-systole}
\end{equation}
\end{lemma}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "known_construction_input_found", "full_statement_found": false, "locator": "Original Lemmas4.2–4.3, Theorem4.5, Propositions4.6–4.7 and Corollary4.8 p30; sphere recognition Theorem8.1. Prior exact full-read scopes retained.", "relation": "Known underlying marked complex torus/sphere family and cusp/finite-fillings data only. The trivial rank-two cusp quotient follows from the existing image/kernel monodromy lattice; the receiving lemma writes the actual flat map, integral kernel and radial isometry. It is an explicit application to the marked family.", "terms_searched": ["vanishing.*cycle", "cusp.*quotient", "invariant.*quotient", "real.*torus"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/carrier_credit/searches_164.json#cusp-cone-native-descent|AC26", "searched_file": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "searched_sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 4, "context_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/carrier_credit/context_readings.json#AC26"}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "known_construction_input_found", "full_statement_found": false, "locator": "Original torus/sphere construction; Lemma3.8 (source842–850) and Remark8.3 (1685–1723) for the invariant-circle antecedent.", "relation": "Known underlying marked complex torus/sphere family and cusp/finite-fillings data only. The trivial rank-two cusp quotient follows from the existing image/kernel monodromy lattice; the receiving lemma writes the actual flat map, integral kernel and radial isometry. It is an explicit application to the marked family.", "terms_searched": ["vanishing.*cycle", "cusp.*quotient", "invariant.*quotient", "real.*torus"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/carrier_credit/searches_164.json#cusp-cone-native-descent|E26", "searched_file": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "searched_sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13