{"row_key": "working_edition:cusp-cone-S12-route", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "wb:cusp-cone-S12-route", "source_file": "sources/workbench/cusp_cone_sphere_routes.tex", "source_line": 36453, "source_section": "Local covers, global quotients and cusp carriers", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Theorem", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}[Exact localized \(S^{12}\) route]
\label{wb:cusp-cone-S12-route}
Choose \(x_0\in W\), and base \(\mathcal A\) at \(v_0\).  There is a
continuous surjective based quotient map
\begin{equation}
 q_2:(X,x_0)\longrightarrow(\mathcal A,v_0)
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-q2}
\end{equation}
with the following exact description.  For \(x\in N_0\setminus W\), write
\[
 t(f(x))=re^{i\phi},\qquad 0<r<\epsilon,
\]
and let \(\overline\pi_f(x)\in\overline T^2\) be the fibre component of
\(\overline\pi(x)\).  Then
\begin{equation}
 q_2(x)=[r,e^{i\phi},\overline\pi_f(x)],\qquad
 q_2(W)=v_0,\qquad
 q_2\bigl(X\setminus\operatorname{int}N_0\bigr)=v_1.
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-q2-formula}
\end{equation}
On \(f^{-1}(|t|=\epsilon)\), the value is \(v_1\).

The smash square is a global based map
\begin{equation}
 q_2^{\wedge2}:X\wedge X\longrightarrow
 \mathcal A\wedge\mathcal A.
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-S12-map}
\end{equation}
Using \(X\cong_{\mathrm{diff}}S^6\), a based choice of the diffeomorphism
identifies its source with
\begin{equation}
 X\wedge X\cong S^6\wedge S^6\cong S^{12}.
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-S12-source}
\end{equation}
For \(0<e^{-2\pi T}<\epsilon\), the canonical product-to-smash quotient
maps restrict to embeddings on \(F_T^2\) and on the corresponding interior
target-product cross-section.  Under those embeddings and \(\iota_T^2\),
the induced smash map restricts exactly to
\begin{equation}
 \pi_T\times\pi_T:F_T\times F_T\longrightarrow Q_T\times Q_T.
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-S12-fibre-map}
\end{equation}
With the Euclidean \(\ell^2\)-product flat quotient metric,
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{sys}(Q_T\times Q_T)\geq T-C,\qquad
 (Q_T\times Q_T,(0,0))\longrightarrow(\mathbb R^4,0)
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-S12-R4-limit}
\end{equation}
in pointed local-isometric, pointed smooth, and pointed
Gromov--Hausdorff topology.  Once \(T-C>4R\), the radius-\(R\) ball is
exactly Euclidean.

The integral homology of the targets is
\begin{equation}
 \widetilde H_k(\mathcal A;\mathbb Z)\cong
 \begin{cases}
  \mathbb Z^3,&k=2,3,\\
  \mathbb Z,&k=4,\\
  0,&\text{otherwise},
 \end{cases}
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-A-homology}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \widetilde H_k(\mathcal A\wedge\mathcal A;\mathbb Z)\cong
 \begin{cases}
  \mathbb Z^9,&k=4,\\
  \mathbb Z^{18},&k=5,\\
  \mathbb Z^{15},&k=6,\\
  \mathbb Z^6,&k=7,\\
  \mathbb Z,&k=8,\\
  0,&\text{otherwise}.
 \end{cases}
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-A-smash-homology}
\end{equation}
In particular, the target is not \(S^4\), \(S^{12}\), or a compact
four-manifold.
\end{theorem}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "known_construction_input_found", "full_statement_found": false, "locator": "Original Lemmas4.2–4.3, Theorem4.5, Propositions4.6–4.7 and Corollary4.8 p30; sphere recognition Theorem8.1. Prior exact full-read scopes retained.", "relation": "Known underlying marked complex torus/sphere family and cusp/finite-fillings data only. The localized retained-angle quotient, exact radial restriction and target are specified constructions. Sphere smash identities, suspension homology and the Kunneth computation are classical; no matching full marked construction was found in the compared contexts.", "terms_searched": ["S.?12", "smash", "suspension", "cone.*torus"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/carrier_credit/searches_164.json#cusp-cone-S12-route|AC26", "searched_file": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "searched_sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 1, "context_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/carrier_credit/context_readings.json#AC26"}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "known_construction_input_found", "full_statement_found": false, "locator": "Original torus/sphere construction; Lemma3.8 (source842–850) and Remark8.3 (1685–1723) for the invariant-circle antecedent.", "relation": "Known underlying marked complex torus/sphere family and cusp/finite-fillings data only. The localized retained-angle quotient, exact radial restriction and target are specified constructions. Sphere smash identities, suspension homology and the Kunneth computation are classical; no matching full marked construction was found in the compared contexts.", "terms_searched": ["S.?12", "smash", "suspension", "cone.*torus"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/carrier_credit/searches_164.json#cusp-cone-S12-route|E26", "searched_file": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "searched_sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfd