{"row_key": "working_edition:cusp-cone-metric-scope", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "wb:cusp-cone-metric-scope", "source_file": "sources/workbench/cusp_cone_sphere_routes.tex", "source_line": 36938, "source_section": "Local covers, global quotients and cusp carriers", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Proposition", "source_statement": "\begin{proposition}[Intrinsic expansion versus ambient collapse]
\label{wb:cusp-cone-metric-scope}
Let \(D_{12}\), \(D_{24}^{\mathcal B}\), and
\(D_{24}^{\mathcal C}\) be arbitrary fixed metrics compatible with the
topologies of \(\mathcal A^{\wedge2}\), \(\mathcal B^{\wedge4}\), and
\(\mathcal C^{\wedge4}\), respectively.  In their corresponding ambient
metrics, the radial target
slices satisfy
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{diam}_{\mathrm{amb}}
 \bigl(j_T(Q_T^2)\bigr)\longrightarrow0,\qquad
 \operatorname{diam}_{\mathrm{amb}}
 \bigl(k_T^{\mathcal B}(C_T^4)\bigr)\longrightarrow0,\qquad
 \operatorname{diam}_{\mathrm{amb}}
 \bigl(k_T^{\mathcal C}(C_T^4)\bigr)\longrightarrow0.
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-ambient-collapse}
\end{equation}
By contrast, in the intrinsic quotient metrics,
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{diam}(Q_T^2)\geq\tfrac12(T-C)\longrightarrow\infty,\qquad
 \operatorname{diam}(C_T^4)\geq\tfrac12\ell_T\longrightarrow\infty.
 \label{wb:cusp-cone-intrinsic-expansion}
\end{equation}
Thus \cref{wb:cusp-cone-S12-R4-limit} and \cref{wb:cusp-cone-S24-R4-limit} assert
intrinsic, flat pointed limits of varying slices, not Sormani--Wenger
intrinsic-flat convergence and not an ambient pointed \(\mathbb R^4\) limit
inside one fixed compact metric target.
\end{proposition}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "{"status": "known_construction_input_found", "full_statement_found": false, "locator": "Original Lemmas4.2–4.3, Theorem4.5, Propositions4.6–4.7 and Corollary4.8 p30; sphere recognition Theorem8.1. Prior exact full-read scopes retained.", "relation": "Known underlying marked complex torus/sphere family and cusp/finite-fillings data only. Uniform collapse at a cone endpoint and boundedness of a compatible compact metric are classical topological facts. The exact intrinsic systolic growth is the marked period calculation; the combined scope statement concerns these particular slices.", "terms_searched": ["ambient", "intrinsic", "systol", "Gromov"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/carrier_credit/searches_164.json#cusp-cone-metric-scope|AC26", "searched_file": "sources/external/root/AC26_pdf_text.txt", "searched_sha256": "e3a403c0ef610e2aefb22f56b59dd495931dc7015b045cdc30f1403a31a65040", "hit_count": 1, "context_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/carrier_credit/context_readings.json#AC26"}", "found_in_E26": "{"status": "known_construction_input_found", "full_statement_found": false, "locator": "Original torus/sphere construction; Lemma3.8 (source842–850) and Remark8.3 (1685–1723) for the invariant-circle antecedent.", "relation": "Known underlying marked complex torus/sphere family and cusp/finite-fillings data only. Uniform collapse at a cone endpoint and boundedness of a compatible compact metric are classical topological facts. The exact intrinsic systolic growth is the marked period calculation; the combined scope statement concerns these particular slices.", "terms_searched": ["ambient", "intrinsic", "systol", "Gromov"], "search_record": "deliverables/work/cdp_audit/carrier_credit/searches_164.json#cusp-cone-metric-scope|E26", "searched_file": "sources/papers/arXiv_2609.38442_Engel_src/S6.tex", "searched_sha256": "95ea78327c33351d609a3001539756f0043dfdef13a37a81927608c953c98c36",