{"row_key": "WORKING_EDITION_COURSE_PROVIDER:CG-S6-PF-THEOREM-5.1", "source_compendium_paper": "I", "source_compendium_label": "mapsI:pf:theorem:5.1", "source_file": "sources/codex_workspace/courses/CG-S6/src/path-fibres-and-integral-homotopy-equivalences.md:371", "source_line": 31598, "source_section": "Path fibres and integral homotopy equivalences", "placement_basis": "plan §3 classical/course material", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Classical rederivation", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}
\label{mapsI:pf:theorem:5.1}
Let \(f:A\to B\) be an integral homology equivalence between path-connected, simply connected spaces with specified CW homotopy comparisons. Then \(f\) is a homotopy equivalence. The construction below gives the inverse through those comparisons, rather than replacing \(f\) by an unspecified map.
\end{theorem}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "Classical prerequisite or worked teaching example, not claimed new and not attributed to this construction paper. Its complete receiving proof is printed and independently read; no result-specific negative literature-absence assertion is made.", "found_in_E26": "Classical prerequisite or worked teaching example, not claimed new and not attributed to this construction paper. Its complete receiving proof is printed and independently read; no result-specific negative literature-absence assertion is made.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "Classical prerequisite or worked teaching example, not claimed new and not attributed to this construction paper. Its complete receiving proof is printed and independently read; no result-specific negative literature-absence assertion is made.", "found_elsewhere": "Known: Hatcher, Algebraic Topology (2002), Corollary 4.33, pp.367–368, original statement and proof opened; simply connected CW type and integral homology equivalence matched. The complete actual-map path-fibre proof is printed."}, "historical_source_notes": "Added prerequisite row; preserves all initial 928 inventory rows. Source SHA256 56799fbbd300a7ec7d0df46ff408010dbd36817f0cc058a16008566b5df3128d; audit work/maps_audit/paperI_course_foundations_manifest.json; portable finite checkers supplement, and do not replace, the full proofs."}

