{"row_key": "WORKING_EDITION_COURSE_PROVIDER:CG-S6-FRAMED6-8", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "courseIII:framed6:8", "source_file": "sources/codex_workspace/courses/CG-S6/src/the-original-six-dimensional-framing-invariant.md", "source_line": 63021, "source_section": "The original six-dimensional framing obstruction", "placement_basis": "plan §3 classical/course material", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Classical proved construction", "source_statement": "\label{courseIII:framed6:8}

We first prove the change across an actual stage of index-three handles, then reduce an arbitrary framed bordism between two-connected six-manifolds to two such stages. The reduction needs vanishing in relative degree two, not an assumption that the whole bordism is a homology equivalence.
