Write \(r=d-2=(p-1)+(q-1)\), and use the auxiliary model coordinates

\begin{equation}
(x,y,z_A,z_B)\in
 \mathbb R^2\times\mathbb R^{p-1}\times\mathbb R^{q-1}.
 \label{courseIII:whitney-moves-in-the-receiving-dimensions:eq:4.1}
\end{equation}

The original two-dimensional disk-to-model comparison is constructed in \cref{courseIII:whitney-move-with-controlled-support:section-3} and \cref{courseIII:whitney-move-with-controlled-support:section-4} of the \cref{courseIII:whitney-move-with-controlled-support:move-original-disk}. It is a comparison of two-dimensional corner disks and their full collars, so its formulas have no ambient-rank dependence. Retain its arbitrary positive \(R\), both original corner germs, its polar radius and its complete collar-extension map. In this model put

\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
 \phi(x)&=R^2-x^2,\\
 D_R&=\{(x,y,0,0):-R\leq x\leq R,\ 0\leq y\leq\phi(x)\},\\
 A_0&=\{(x,\phi(x),z_A,0)\},\qquad
 B_0=\{(x,0,0,z_B)\}.
 \end{aligned}
 \label{courseIII:whitney-moves-in-the-receiving-dimensions:eq:4.2}
\end{equation}

Let \(\psi_D:D_R\to D\) be that complete original disk comparison. Its normal rank here is \(r\), with \(r=3\) or \(4\).
