Their supports are disjoint. The drawing is one coordinate section of the collar, with the roof values and the common critical value distinguished; it does not place the whole handles inside that section. The right panel is the invariant section with every coordinate except \(x_2,y_2\) equal to zero. Its contours retain the original coefficients \(11,13\), and its arrows show one third of the actual ascending vector. All omitted coordinate contributions remain in \eqref{courseIII:realizing-framed-handles-and-middle-cancellation:eq:2.9} and \eqref{courseIII:realizing-framed-handles-and-middle-cancellation:eq:7.7}. The lower panel records the proved bijection \eqref{courseIII:realizing-framed-handles-and-middle-cancellation:eq:4.7}, followed by the exact dimension-dependent cancellation order of \cref{courseIII:realizing-framed-handles-and-middle-cancellation:section-6}. The complete figure source is reproducible; no additional result is inferred from its numerical samples.
