 =\mathbb Z(e_1+e_2+e_3)\oplus\mathbb Z e_4.
 \label{courseIII:removing-the-original-zero-and-top-handles:eq:6.2}
\end{equation}

The root-to-\(q_1\) edge supplies a geometric zero/one cancellation by \cref{courseIII:removing-the-original-zero-and-top-handles:section-3}. Repeating the actual construction removes two minima and two index-one points. Equation \eqref{courseIII:removing-the-original-zero-and-top-handles:eq:3.4} leaves two index-one points, in agreement with the two retained independent cycle vectors. The algebra calculation does not identify those surviving critical points with a preselected geometric basis of the two cycles; the intervening diffeomorphisms and fields determine that comparison.
