{"row_key": "WORKING_EDITION_COURSE_PROVIDER:CG-S6-MILNOR-COBAR-7.2", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "courseIII:milnor-cobar:7.2", "source_file": "sources/codex_workspace/courses/CG-S6/src/the-degree-six-milnor-cobar-calculation.md", "source_line": 57502, "source_section": "The degree-six calculation in the full Milnor cobar complex", "placement_basis": "plan §3 classical/course material", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Classical worked example", "source_statement": "\label{courseIII:milnor-cobar:7.2}

At \(p=3\), find a complete preimage of \([X|T_0|X]\).

\textbf{Solution.} In this case \eqref{courseIII:the-degree-six-milnor-cobar-calculation:eq:6.3} gives \(|[X]|_{\rm tot}=3\) and \(|[T_0]|_{\rm tot}=0\). A suitable length-two cochain is

\begin{equation}
Z=[T_0X|X]+\frac12[T_0|X^2].
 \label{courseIII:the-degree-six-milnor-cobar-calculation:eq:7.4}
\end{equation}

Indeed

\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
 d[T_0X|X]&=-[T_0|X|X]+[X|T_0|X],\\
 d\!\left(\frac12[T_0|X^2]\right)
   &=\frac12\cdot2[T_0|X|X]=[T_0|X|X].
\end{aligned}
\label{courseIII:the-degree-six-milnor-cobar-calculation:eq:7.5}
\end{equation}

Their sum is exactly the required word. The coefficient \(1/2\), the negative term and its cancellation are all essential parts of the original differential.

