{"row_key": "WORKING_EDITION_COURSE_PROVIDER:CG-S6-DUALITY-3.2", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "courseIII:duality:3.2", "source_file": "sources/codex_workspace/courses/CG-S6/sources/manifold-duality-the-diagonal-and-wu-classes.source.txt", "source_line": 43036, "source_section": "Singular duality, the diagonal and the Euler class", "placement_basis": "plan §3 classical/course material", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Classical theorem", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}[Tubular neighbourhood]
\label{courseIII:duality:3.2}
If \(M\subset A\) is a smooth embedded submanifold, its normal quotient bundle \(\nu=TA|_M/TM\) has a neighbourhood of its zero section diffeomorphic to an open neighbourhood of \(M\) in \(A\), fixing \(M\). The whole bundle is diffeomorphic to such a neighbourhood by a radial fibre change. If \(M\) is closed as a subset of \(A\), excision also identifies the pairs' cohomology


\begin{equation}
H^*(A,A\setminus M;R)\cong H^*(\nu,\nu\setminus M;R).
\label{courseIII:manifold-duality-the-diagonal-and-wu-classes.source:eq:3.2}
\end{equation}


\end{theorem}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "Found applications of Poincare duality/UCT and top Chern=Euler in AC26 §§7–9, with a trivial-normal Thom isomorphism in AppendixB. This is classical prior input, not a new result of the course. The exact compact-support/signed-diagonal proof is a retained independent proof.", "found_in_E26": "Found Poincare duality/UCT applications, including source1408/1641 and main sphere proof. No complete signed-diagonal/compact-support proof identified.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "The diagonal hit at768 is a period-matrix determinant, not this Poincare-duality construction.", "found_elsewhere": "Classical singular duality, Thom/Euler and signed-diagonal formulas; exact Milnor–Stasheff source and Hatcher prerequisites opened. Full chain-level receiving proofs and the exact original producer headers are retained."}, "historical_source_notes": "Keep this exact provider proof once. Several earlier geometric arguments rederive special cases; those are distinct coordinate proofs. Do not import unread Wu-class material. Source SHA256 ab25518584fbd117254b90d0008a602bc69a222169e7e520b9c128b749dd4aea; full retained proof deliverables/work/maps_audit/checked_course_providers/manifold-duality-through-euler.md; reserved label courseIII:duality:3.2. Producer: GPT-6.1 Sol (OpenAI), effort Ultra, October 2026 (no day recorded). Full raw producer provenance and ranges are retained in the provider inventory. | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json | Separate DGKXv2 comparison: No matching duality/Thom/Euler proof located by the recorded terms. | Final bounded source comparison: work/maps_audit/course249_credit_comparison.json"}

{"row_key": "WORKING_EDITION_COURSE_PROVIDER:CG-S6-DUALITY-3.3", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "courseIII:duality:3.3", "source_file": "sources/codex_workspace/courses/CG-S6/sources/manifold-duality-the-diagonal-and-wu-classes.source.txt", "source_line": 43066, "source_section": "Singular duality, the diagonal and the Euler class", "placement_basis": "plan §3 classical/course material", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Classical lemma", "source_statement": "\begin{lemma}[Compact Euclidean embedding and finite domination]
\label{courseIII:duality:3.3}
Every compact smooth manifold embeds smoothly in some finite Euclidean space and is a retract of a neighbourhood there. Its integer homology is finitely generated and vanishes in sufficiently large degrees, whether or not it is oriented.
\end{lemma}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "Found applications of Poincare duality/UCT and top Chern=Euler in AC26 §§7–9, with a trivial-normal Thom isomorphism in AppendixB. This is classical prior input, not a new result of the course. The exact compact-support/signed-diagonal proof is a retained independent proof.", "found_in_E26": "Found Poincare duality/UCT applications, including source1408/1641 and main sphere proof. No complete signed-diagonal/compact-support proof identified.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "The diagonal hit at768 is a period-matrix determinant, not this Poincare-duality construction.", "found_elsewhere": "Classical singular duality, Thom/Euler and signed-diagonal formulas; exact Milnor–Stasheff source and Hatcher prerequisites opened. Full chain-level receiving proofs and the exact original producer headers are retained."}, "historical_source_notes": "Keep this exact provider proof once. Several earlier geometric arguments rederive special cases; those are distinct coordinate proofs. Do not import unread Wu-class material. Source SHA256 ab25518584fbd117254b90d0008a602bc69a222169e7e520b9c128b749dd4aea; full retained proof deliverables/work/maps_audit/checked_course_providers/manifold-duality-through-euler.md; reserved label courseIII:duality:3.3. Producer: GPT-6.1 Sol (OpenAI), effort Ultra, October 2026 (no day recorded). Full raw producer provenance and ranges are retained in the provider inventory. | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json | Separate DGKXv2 comparison: No matching duality/Thom/Euler proof located by the recorded terms. | Final bounded source comparison: work/maps_audit/course249_credit_comparison.json"}

{"row_key": "WORKING_EDITION_COURSE_PROVIDER:CG-S6-DUALITY-4.1", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "courseIII:duality:4.1", "source_file": "sources/codex_workspace/courses/CG-S6/sources/manifold-duality-the-diagonal-and-wu-classes.source.txt", "source_line": 43146, "source_section": "Singular duality, the diagonal and the Euler class", "placement_basis": "plan §3 classical/course material", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Classical theorem", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}[The signed diagonal formula]
\label{courseIII:duality:4.1}
Work over a field \(F\), with \(M\) oriented or with \(F=\mathbb F _2\). Choose a homogeneous basis \(b_i\) of \(H^*(M;F)\), and its cup-dual basis \(b_i^\vee\) satisfying


\[
\langle b_i\smile b_j^\vee,[M]\rangle=\delta_{ij}.
\]


Then


\begin{equation}
U=\sum_i(-1)^{|b_i|}\,b_i\times b_i^\vee.
\label{courseIII:manifold-duality-the-diagonal-and-wu-classes.source:eq:4.5}
\end{equation}


\end{theorem}", "historical_literature_checks": {"found_in_AC26": "Found applications of Poincare duality/UCT and top Chern=Euler in AC26 §§7–9, with a trivial-normal Thom isomorphism in AppendixB. This is classical prior input, not a new result of the course. The exact compact-support/signed-diagonal proof is a retained independent proof.", "found_in_E26": "Found Poincare duality/UCT applications, including source1408/1641 and main sphere proof. No complete signed-diagonal/compact-support proof identified.", "found_in_DGKX_v1": "The diagonal hit at768 is a period-matrix determinant, not this Poincare-duality construction.", "found_elsewhere": "Classical singular duality, Thom/Euler and signed-diagonal formulas; exact Milnor–Stasheff source and Hatcher prerequisites opened. Full chain-level receiving proofs and the exact original producer headers are retained."}, "historical_source_notes": "Keep this exact provider proof once. Several earlier geometric arguments rederive special cases; those are distinct coordinate proofs. Do not import unread Wu-class material. Source SHA256 ab25518584fbd117254b90d0008a602bc69a222169e7e520b9c128b749dd4aea; full retained proof deliverables/work/maps_audit/checked_course_providers/manifold-duality-through-euler.md; reserved label courseIII:duality:4.1. Producer: GPT-6.1 Sol (OpenAI), effort Ultra, October 2026 (no day recorded). Full raw producer provenance and ranges are retained in the provider inventory. | Final receiving/dependency event: work/maps_audit/III_final_closure_overlay.json | Separate DGKXv2 comparison: No matching duality/Thom/Euler proof located by the recorded terms. | Final bounded source comparison: work/maps_audit/course249_credit_comparison.json"}

{"row_key": "WORKING_EDITION_COURSE_PROVIDER:CG-S6-DUALITY-4.2", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "courseIII:duality:4.2", "source_file": "sources/codex_workspace/courses/CG-S6/sources/manifold-duality-the-diagonal-and-wu-classes.source.txt", "source_line": 43202, "source_section": "Singular duality, the diagonal and the Euler class", "placement_basis": "plan §3 classical/course material", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Classical corollary", "source_statement": "\begin{corollary}[Euler number and Euler characteristic]
\label{courseIII:duality:4.2}
For a closed oriented manifold,


\begin{equation}
\langle e(TM),[M]\rangle=\chi(M).
\label{courseIII:manifold-duality-the-diagonal-and-wu-classes.source:eq:4.7}
\end{equation}


For every closed manifold,


\begin{equation}
\langle w_d(TM),[M]_2\rangle\equiv\chi(M)\pmod2.
\label{courseIII:manifold-duality-the-diagonal-and-wu-classes.source:eq:4.8}
\end{equation}


