{"row_key": "working_edition:sphere-metric-uniform-collapse", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "wb:sphere-metric-uniform-collapse", "source_file": "sources/overleaf_working_edition/supporting_materials/workbench/research/cusp_sphere_fixed_metric.tex", "source_line": 39082, "source_section": "Local covers, global quotients and cusp carriers", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Theorem", "source_statement": "\begin{theorem}[Topology-forced collapse for every fixed compatible metric]
\label{wb:sphere-metric-uniform-collapse}
Let \(D_{12},D_{24}^{\mathcal B},D_{24}^{\mathcal C}\) be arbitrary fixed
metrics compatible with the respective compact target topologies, and let
\(*\) denote the corresponding smash base point.  Then
\begin{align}
 d_H^{D_{12}}\bigl(j_T(Q_T^2),\{*\}\bigr)&\longrightarrow0,\\
 d_H^{D_{24}^{\mathcal B}}
  \bigl(k_T^{\mathcal B}(C_T^4),\{*\}\bigr)&\longrightarrow0,\\
 d_H^{D_{24}^{\mathcal C}}
  \bigl(k_T^{\mathcal C}(C_T^4),\{*\}\bigr)&\longrightarrow0.
 \label{wb:sphere-metric-Hausdorff-collapse}
\end{align}
Consequently, with the metrics restricted from any one fixed ambient
target, all three target slices converge in Gromov--Hausdorff topology to
a point, not to \(\mathbb R^4\).
