{"row_key": "working_edition:h24:ret:orientation-lemma", "source_compendium_paper": "III", "source_compendium_label": "wb:h24:ret:orientation-lemma", "source_file": "sources/workbench/higher_rung_24d_continuation.tex", "source_line": 40298, "source_section": "Local covers, global quotients and cusp carriers", "placement_basis": "candidate body placement; source-credit and proof reviews pending", "placement_state": "provisional editorial mapping; no current mathematical validation inferred", "source_kind": "Lemma", "source_statement": "\begin{lemma}[The exact orientation sign]\label{wb:h24:ret:orientation-lemma}
Use the complex real-coordinate orientation, whose ordered coordinates are
\[
 (\operatorname{Re}w_0,\operatorname{Im}w_0,
  \operatorname{Re}w_1,\operatorname{Im}w_1,
  \operatorname{Re}w_2,\operatorname{Im}w_2).
\]
Then one has
\begin{equation}
 \det(N_\ell,N_\phi,N_1,N_2,T_a,T_b)
       =-\det(A_0)|w_0w_1w_2|^2<0.
 \label{wb:h24:ret:eq:sign}
\end{equation}
Hence the tangent orientation induced by the ordered normal frame is
